\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2012\par 18:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par US STOCKS EDGE LOWER AFTER RALLY, EURO-ZONE WORRIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks move lower as euro-zone liquidity concerns prompt investors to consolidate some of the sharp gains registered a day earlier. The Dow Jones Industrial Average is off more than 50 points.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US AUTO MAKERS SEE 2011 SALES GAINS INTENSIFYING IN 2012 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Auto makers cap off 2011 with strong a strong December and now expect the recovery in U.S. sales to intensify in 2012 as a stabilizing economy and ongoing job creation continue to encourage shoppers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US NOVEMBER FACTORY ORDERS RISE 1.8% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Factory orders increase for the first time in three months on greater demand for aircraft and other goods, the latest indication the manufacturing sector is slowly gaining momentum. Orders rise to $459.18 billion; economists were expecting an increase of 2.1%.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -TRADE CONTROVERSY SWELLS AROUND SNB PRESIDENT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A controversy surrounding transactions made by the wife of Swiss National Bank President Philipp Hildebrand swells after media reports that he profited from a large dollar purchase around the time of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INVESTORS LOSING CONFIDENCE IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HUNGARY\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors' confidence in the Hungarian government is evaporating, sharply raising pressure on policy makers here as they struggle to contain the spreading economic damage from the Continent's debt woes and stalling euro-zone growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL SLIPS AMID EU BAN OF IRANIAN OIL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although oil prices spiked in mid-morning trading to highest level in nearly eight months on reports that EU officials agreed in principal to an embargo on Iranian oil imports, they fall back on an apparent lack of concrete details.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANKS PARK RECORD FUNDS WITH ECB \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European banks parked a record amount of funds at the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's overnight deposit facility Tuesday while short-term emergency borrowing from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained elevated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREEK PM EXPECTS DEBT PLAN DEVELOPMENT IN 15 DAYS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Greek government appears to be nearing a deal with banks in negotiations on writing down their Greek bonds, a union leader says, citing Prime Minister Lucas Papademos.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MORTGAGE APPLICATION VOLUME FALLS 3.7% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of mortgage applications filed in the U.S. falls 3.7%, the Mortgage Bankers Association says, even after adjusting for the seasonal effects of the Christmas and New Year's holidays.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB BALANCE SHEET GROWS SLIGHTLY, GOLD RESERVES INCREASE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Eurosystem's balance sheet grows slightly, topping a previous all-time high as the ECB continues buying government bonds on the secondary market and as the value of its gold reserves increases.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Election 2012 \par ROMNEY WINS IOWA CAUCUSES BY EIGHT VOTES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitt Romney pulls out a razor-thin victory by just eight votes in the Iowa caucuses, edging out former Pennsylvania Sen. Rick Santorum with a dose of momentum going into a New Hampshire primary he is heavily favored to win.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Analysis \par PIMCO'S GROSS: BUY TREASURYS, AVOID EURO ZONE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After getting burned by selling Treasury securities in the early part of 2011, bond investor Bill Gross is placing the asset class at the top of his shopping list for 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par The Wall Street Journal \par HUNGARY WILLING TO BE FLEXIBLE IN EU, IMF TALKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungarian economic officials stress their willingness to be flexible in negotiations with the EU and IMF over a precautionary credit line the country is seeking as insurance against market turmoil.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TRANSFER PAYMENTS WON'T RESCUE THE EURO ZONE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The divide between the German and Spanish economies fuels the argument that a single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  needs a single fiscal policy, including fiscal transfers. But as the U.K. has demonstrated, fiscal transfers can actually prevent economic readjustment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCKS EDGE LOWER AFTER STRONG RALLY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks move lower amid fresh concerns over euro-zone liquidity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TREASURYS TURN LOWER AMID CORPORATE-DEBT SALES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys turn lower amid hedging linked to corporate-bond supply.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO BRIEFLY FALLS BELOW $1.29 AS RISK AVERSION GRIPS MARKET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro down against dollar as risk aversion returns.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE TURNS CHOPPY ON EU BAN OF IRANIAN OIL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil futures slip on apparent lack of details about EU ban of Iranian oil.\f28 \par \par \uc2 