\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE Hungary Won't Allow Outside Interference In Lawmaking -PM\b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2011\par 11:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Hungary PM determined to go ahead with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill ratification\par \par \uc2 --PM Orban continues to reject foreign calls to change domestic policies\par \par \uc2 --Hungary \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  questions legitimacy of new bill prior to ratification \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Gergo Racz \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (rewrites throughout, adds details, background, comments from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and analyst)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't allow outside forces to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the country's policymaking, Prime Minister Viktor Orban said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is no person in the world who could tell elected representatives of the Hungarian people what laws they can or can't create," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Orban reacted to criticism targeted at the government from abroad, including calls from European Commission President Jose Manual Barroso and United States Secretary of State Hilary Clinton to amend bills submitted to Parliament. Pieces of legislation revising the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  proved a dealbreaker earlier this month when delegations from the International Monetary Fund and the European Union terminated negotiations early with the Hungarian government.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If Hungary's parliament were to create a law that would be in breach of the country's obligations laid out in international treaties, than the aggrieved party may take steps, but only after ratification, not before," Orban said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bill allows the government to delegate new members to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rate-setting council while another, related bill allows merging the finance market regulator and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . In this case, the current post of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor would be demoted to deputy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The laws about to be passed go against legal security and allow the government to realize its short-term political goals through influencing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision-making," the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Hungary\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday, prior to parliament's closing vote in the matter. "It hurts the economic interests and stability of the country," the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the apparently rigid negotiating positions, PM Orban said Hungary's delegation will conduct talks with the IMF sometime at the start of January.He added, however, there is no fixed schedule yet, and stressed that an agreement with the Fund isn't a necessity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Hungary has an excellent budget for 2012 and the country can stand on its own without the IMF," he said on public radio.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, markets would apparently be more confident regarding Hungary's outlooks if it had the IMF in its corner, as reflected by an unsuccessful government bond auction on Thursday and the continued weakness of the national \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Investors are rapidly losing confidence in Hungarian policymaking and are beginning to shun the country's bond market. The standoff is escalating by the day and unless negotiations with the IMF resume and a workable agreement is reached fairly quickly, Hungary will have a full-blown debt crisis on its hands," said Nicholas Spiro, managing director at Spiro Sovereign Strategy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Parliament is set to ratify the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bill later Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Gergo Racz, Dow Jones Newswires, +36 30 452 3980; gergo.racz@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 30, 2011 05:52 ET (10:52 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111230e7cu001xv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
