\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3- \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  debt yields jump, Poland talks of new  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 952 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2011\par 17:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Polish cbanker, updates levels)\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets fragile, Polish cbank warns may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again\par \par \uc2 * Czech, Polish debt stable after selloff; \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  down\par \par \uc2 * Spreading euro zone crisis weighs\par \par \uc2 By Sandor Peto\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST/WARSAW, Nov 24 (Reuters) - Hungarian bond yields soared to 2-1/2 year highs on Thursday and Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned of further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained under pressure on concerns the euro zone debt crisis is threatening even Germany.\par \par \uc2 The yield at an auction of 12-month Hungarian Treasury bills rose to its highest since September 2009, at 7.07 percent, although the debt agency managed to sell all 30 billion forints of paper on offer.\par \par \uc2 On secondary bond markets, Hungarian yields rose up to 20 basis points to highs last seen in the summer of 2009 following a similar rise in the previous session, when a German bond auction described as "disastrous" hit central European debt.\par \par \uc2 "We saw an almost continuous rise in yields," one Budapest-based fixed income trader said. "I hope this will not continue next week as that would already be real big trouble... European markets are in a panic which has spilled over into our market."\par \par \uc2 "I hope things will improve next week when U.S. investors return from their holidays," he added.\par \par \uc2 Hungary has been the central European market most vulnerable to investors cutting back their exposure to risk, and the forint, which lost more than 1 percent on Wednesday, stayed near record lows, slipping 0.3 percent to 310.99 per euro.\par \par \uc2 In Poland, where the zloty hovered close to multi-month lows, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Reuters it was likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again after stepping into the market on Wednesday for the fourth time in less than three months.\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was nearly flat at 4.49, a nudge below the key psychological level of 4.50 and year-lows just beyond.\par \par \uc2 "The comments by the deputy governor temporarily supported the zloty," one Warsaw trader said. "I think a further retreat of the zloty towards this year's minimum of 4.42-4.53 to the euro is still possible."\par \par \uc2 "The question is whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will defend these levels," he added.\par \par \uc2 Both the zloty and forint have lost more than 10 percent in 2011, mostly in the latter half of the year.\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown slipped 0.4 percent against the euro to 25.76, and a Prague-based dealer said it could be heading towards 26.300-500 if it stays weaker than 25.300-400, an area that has offered support.\par \par \uc2 A Hungarian dealer said the forint had no room to firm in the short term as concerns remain that \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  may cut Hungary's debt rating to junk even though the government has applied to the IMF for a precautionary credit line.\par \par \uc2 "The forint has almost lost all its gains posted since the news about the (planned) IMF deal, but can firm in the longer term on the news flow about the talks and the deal," another dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Romania's leu, which has seen support from prospects of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  there, firmed 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Fears that the worsening euro zone sovereign debt crisis will cripple economic activity, leaving central Europe's export-reliant economies vulnerable, have hammered the region's markets.\par \par \uc2 The Czech 10-year yield was quoted up 6 bps at 4.489 pct\par \par \uc2 after a jump of 40 basis points on Wednesday in a usually stable market.\par \par \uc2 The region's main equity indices were little changed.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2011 \par Czech crown                 25.763   25.669   -0.36%    -2.96%\par Polish zloty                4.49     4.492    +0.04%    -11.85%\par Hungarian forint            310.99   309.95   -0.33%    -10.61%\par Croatian kuna               7.466    7.491    +0.33%    -1.15%\par Romanian leu                4.354    4.356    +0.05%    -2.78%\par Serbian dinar               103.33   103.15   -0.17%    +2.51%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds           \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR   +3 basis points to  180bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR    -1 basis points to  +219bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ9YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +211bps over bmk*\par Polish treasury bonds           2-yr T-bond   PL2YT=RR   +4 basis points to  +443bps over bmk*5-yr T-bond   PL5YT=RR   +11 basis points to  \par +424bps over bmk*10-yr T-bond PL10YT=RR   +5 basis points to  +391bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds           \par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR   +14 basis points to  +674bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond 