\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Hungary MPC: Uncertainty Around CPI, Econ Projection Higher\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2011\par 14:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 16 Nov 2011 08:04 EDT *DJ  Hungary MPC Divided On Future Monetary Policy Conditions\par \par \uc2 16 Nov 2011 08:07 EDT *DJ  Some Hungary MPC Members: Monetary Policy Can't Offset Euro Zone Crisis\par \par \uc2 16 Nov 2011 08:09 EDT *DJ  Hungary MPC Members Agree In Wait-and-See Monetary Policy Stance\par \par \uc2 16 Nov 2011 08:13 EDT *DJ  Hungary MPC To Assess CPI Outlook After Econ Policy Details Public\par \par \uc2 16 Nov 2011 08:14 EDT *DJ  Hungary MPC To Watch Spillover Effects Of Weak HUF, Taxes In CPI\par \par \uc2 16 Nov 2011 09:17 EDT DJ  Hungary MPC Voted 6 To 1 In Favor Of Oct Rate Hold Decision\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--Six of the seven members of the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council voted in favor of leaving the key rate on hold in October, citing increasing economic headwinds.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept interest rates unchanged at 6%, in line with analysts' expectations. One panel member, Julia Kiraly, wanted to raise rates by 0.25 percentage point, the meeting's minutes showed Wednesday. Kiraly is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor and is in charge of financial stability.\par \par \uc2 The majority of MPC members agreed to adopt a wait-and-see stance, though they were divided over future monetary policy conditions.\par \par \uc2 The bank's lowered its economic outlook because of the country's exposure to the euro-zone debt crisis as well as a government measure aimed at paying off household foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mortgages at the expense of the banking sector. And the MPC agreed to monitor possible inflationary effects stemming from the weak forint and tax changes.\par \par \uc2 It also said it would reassess its mid-term inflation outlooks, once the government finalizes its economic policy, when the bank comes to compile the December inflation forecast.\par \par \uc2 The minutes of the meeting come a day after the MPC verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the forint against further depreciation against the euro, after it hit historic lows around HUF317 Monday. The MPC said that if investor risk aversion persists, this could warrant gradual monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2 The minutes are released two weeks after the rate-setting meeting and therefore don't reflect changes that have occurred in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  period, such as prospective downgrades to \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sovereign rating and forint weakening.\par \par \uc2 -By Gergo Racz and Veronika Gulyas, Dow Jones Newswires; +361-267-0623; veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 16, 2011 09:17 ET (14:17 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020111116e7bg003m2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
