\par\par \b \uc2 Hungary, Factors to watch, Nov 16\b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2011\par 07:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, Nov 16 (Reuters) - Following is a list of events in Hungary and the region, as well as news stories and press reports which may influence financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian press digest is at the end of this item.\par \par \uc2 (For any queries: Budapest editorial +36 1 327 4745)\par \par \uc2 WHAT IS HAPPENING IN HUNGARY (ALL TIMES GMT)\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST - Construction output, Sept (0800)\par \par \uc2 IN THE REGION\par \par \uc2 CZECH - Government meeting (0900)\par \par \uc2 SLOVAKIA - EU-norm inflation 10/11 (0900)\par \par \uc2 CZECH - NWR Q3 results (1100)\par \par \uc2 CZECH - 11-yr bond auction 3.85%/21 (1215)\par \par \uc2 IN THE NEWS REUTERS\par \par \uc2 Hungarians in crisis mood again as forint falls\par \par \uc2 Hammered by the forint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slump to all-time lows, ordinary Hungarians are bracing for another in a long history of market collapses that will drive up the costs of their mortgages and everyday essentials from already crippling levels.\par \par \uc2 Hungary cbank steps in to prop up weak forint\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally on Tuesday to prop up the weak forint, which fell to record lows to the euro late on Monday, and said a gradual tightening of monetary conditions may be needed if risk aversion in European markets is lasting.\par \par \uc2 Banks urge EU to fight Hungary \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan law - letter\par \par \uc2 Top officials at eight big banks have urged the European Commission support them in a dispute with Hungary over a law that saddles lenders with big losses on foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans.\par \par \uc2 East EU GDP grows in Q3, but storm clouds ahead\par \par \uc2 Healthy harvests and exports helped eastern Europe's economies post solid growth in the third quarter, but the region faces stormy waters ahead as the euro zone's debt crisis begins to bite deeper.\par \par \uc2 Govt MP: can't predict if Hungary may need IMF loan-TV\par \par \uc2 A leading politician of Hungary's ruling Fidesz party said on Tuesday he "could not predict" whether the country might need a new loan from the International Monetary Fund (IMF) if the European debt crisis escalates in 2012.\par \par \uc2 HUNGARIAN PRESS\par \par \uc2 ORCO SET TO LEAVE BUDAPEST BOURSE Property developer Orco has asked the BSE to delist its shares, which had been listed on the bourse since 2007.\par \par \uc2 (Hungarian press source: taken from Nepszabadsag's Hungary Around the Clock service. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Gergely Szakacs)\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY-FACTORS/   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111116e7bg0008o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
