\par\par \b \uc2 Hungary, Factors to watch, Oct 7\b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2011\par 07:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, Oct 7 (Reuters) - Following is a list of events in Hungary and the region, as well as news stories and press reports which may influence financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian press digest is at the end of this item.\par \par \uc2 (For any queries: Budapest editorial +36 1 327 4745)\par \par \uc2 WHAT IS HAPPENING IN HUNGARY (ALL TIMES GMT)\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST - Budget balance, Sept (1400)\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST - Cbank end-Sept \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data. (around 0630)\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST - \uc2 Magyar Telekom\uc2  news conference on network development with Chairman and Chief Executive \uc2 Christopher Mattheisen\uc2 . (0830)\par \par \uc2 *BUDAPEST - V4 presidents talk about the economy Presidents of Poland, Hungary, Czech Republic and Slovakia talk about the region's economic outlook at a conference commemorating the 20th anniversary of the founding of the Visegrad Four partnership in Budapest.\par \par \uc2 IN THE REGION\par \par \uc2 CZECH - Industry output data (August) and trade (0700)\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA - Industry output data\par \par \uc2 POLAND - cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data (1200)\par \par \uc2 IN THE NEWS REUTERS\par \par \uc2 POLL-Zloty to lead C.Europe \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovery, short-term shaky The zloty is expected to recover some ground after Polish elections on Sunday and Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should gain over the next year although they remain at risk from deepening turmoil in the euro zone, a Reuters poll showed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Hungary Aug output up 4.4 pct y/y, outlook bleak\par \par \uc2 Hungary's industrial output rose by an annual 4.4 percent in August according to preliminary unadjusted data but fell by 0.4 percent when adjusted for the number of working days, the Central Statistics Office (KSH) said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4-\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreat after ECB offsets \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk\par \par \uc2 Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed gains after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept interest rates at 1.5 percent on Thursday, partly offsetting firming pressure from possible further Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rising share prices.\par \par \uc2 UPDATE 1-Yields fall at \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bond sale\par \par \uc2 Hungary sold government bonds at auctions on Thursday at yields below the secondary market and traders said a recovery of the bonds may continue if comments from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later on Thursday support investors' risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 UPDATE 1-Hungary c.bank chief says rate cuts could hurt economy\par \par \uc2 LONDON - Easing monetary policy could hurt Hungary's economy because of the high foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt exposure of its households and banks, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 HUNGARIAN PRESS FIDESZ CAUCUS UNVEILS ELECTION CONCEPT The Fidesz caucus is recommending a single-round electoral system in which ethnic Hungarians abroad will be granted voting rights, a leaked copy of the concept shows.\par \par \uc2 STUDENTS COUNCIL ANNOUNCES DEMO The National Conference of Students Councils yesterday announced a demonstration in Budapest against the new higher education draft to be held in late October.\par \par \uc2 Councils president D\u225\'00\'E1vid Nagy said the draft ignores the social status of students, while payments for signing undergraduate contracts could be seen as covert tuition fees.\par \par \uc2 BAJNAI'S FOUNDATION TO CLARIFY ECONOMICS The foundation of former prime minister Gordon Bajnai, Haza \u233\'00\'E9s Haladas Alapitvany (Home and Progress Foundation), has launched a website named kozoskassza.hu with the aim of vetting the budget draft and evaluating its impacts.\par \par \uc2 Fiscal analyses will be carried out by former members of the now defunct Budget Council, which wound up its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year after the government slashed its funding.\par \par \uc2 (Hungarian press source: taken from Nepszabadsag's Hungary Around the Clock service. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Krisztina Than)\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY-FACTORS/   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111007e7a70008l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
