\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4-C.banks seen  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  to support zloty, leu\b0\par\par\uc2 1,026 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2011\par 16:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comment, \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  c.bank, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 * Zloty, leu trim losses after cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  c.bank to launch euro sale tenders, seen helping forint\par \par \uc2 * Bond yields rise, stock markets down across board\par \par \uc2 By Sam Cage and Luiza Ilie\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Sept 30 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty and Romanian leu trimmed losses against the euro on Friday after dealers said both countries' central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market to support the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Markets are testing the thresholds at which emerging Europe's central banks will step in to bolster \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit by fears about a spiralling debt crisis in the euro zone -- the region's main trading partner -- and a slowing global economy.\par \par \uc2 The zloty and Hungary's forint have lost 12 percent and 10 percent respectively since July 1.\par \par \uc2 "I think \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be more common if market panic continues," said Nordea's Elisabeth Andreew. "The CEE region has in general much better fundamentals than the euro zone and it is not fundamentally correct that these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be sold off that sharply."\par \par \uc2 "The way it will happen will probably vary though. Poland has a lot of EU funds while I think Hungary for example would do an emergency hike in interest rates if pressure rises too much on the forint."\par \par \uc2 A week ago, Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and state-owned bank BGK launched their first coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed income markets to support the zloty and government bonds, which were pummelled by the global flight from risk.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, two Warsaw dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market selling euros. By 1415 GMT the zloty was quoted at 4.423 against the euro, down 0.2 percent on the day, having earlier traded as much as 0.6 percent lower.\par \par \uc2 Though the Romanian leu has so far been one of the region's most stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its losses have accelerated and it fell to a 15-month low of 4.3725 per euro before dealers cited \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying through local banks which pushed it to 4.353, down 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held rates unchanged at 6.25 percent on Thursday, later suggesting slowing inflation might give room to ease borrowing costs. Finnish handset manufacturer \uc2 Nokia\uc2 's decision to stop production in Romania also damaged sentiment.\par \par \uc2 "I'm thinking this is about as far as the leu goes," a Bucharest dealer said. "A new ceiling for the leu could be 4.38."\par \par \uc2 BOND YIELDS RISE, STOCKS FALL\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the region, Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will launch euro sale tenders on Oct. 3 for commercial banks to help them finance the repayment of households' foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mortgage loans under a government scheme.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the sales would help prevent a plunge in the forint. The bank earlier said that it would use its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to prevent forint volatility as the repayments are seen boosting demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By 1400 GMT the forint was down 0.6 percent on the day, while bond yields rose.\par \par \uc2 "You can see that shorter yields are going up now and long yields are static," one Budapest fixed income trader said.\par \par \uc2 "(Interest rate) swaps keep going up, they are at 6.75 pct for 2 years and 7.00 pct for five years. The markets have clearly priced in two 25 basis point \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate increases for the next one year."\par \par \uc2 The risk-averse mood weakened the Czech crown -- the region's best performer in 2011, down only 1.7 percent since July. It was 0.6 percent down on the day, though it largely shrugged off minutes from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last meeting.\par \par \uc2 The majority of the bank's board believes that risks to the bank's inflation outlook are slightly on the downside, the minutes showed, adding to signs rates may yet head lower.\par \par \uc2 The crown is now weaker than the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's outlook for 24.2 for the third quarter, but analysts said it would tolerate a much deeper fall.\par \par \uc2 Stocks fell across the region with Prague's shedding 1.1 percent and leading losses.\par \par \uc2 In Romania, debt managers said they plan to sell 4 billion lei ($1.3 billion) in domestic debt in October, and analysts will closely follow auctions to see if the finance ministry gets close to its target, as it has struggled to sell debt at yields it deemed acceptable since August. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    clo