\par\par \b \uc2 Hungary, Factors to watch, Sept 28\b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2011\par 08:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, Sept 28 (Reuters) - Following is a list of events in Hungary and the region, as well as news stories and press reports which may influence financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian press digest is at the end of this item.\par \par \uc2 (For any queries: Budapest editorial +36 1 327 4745)\par \par \uc2 WHAT IS HAPPENING IN HUNGARY (ALL TIMES GMT)\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST - Unemployment data June-Aug (0700)\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST - Govt to discuss 2012 draft budget in final reading.\par \par \uc2 IN THE REGION\par \par \uc2 SlOVAKIA - July C/A data\par \par \uc2 POLAND - Polish Finance Minister meets leftist opposition leader to discuss economy ahead of Oct.9 elections.\par \par \uc2 IN THE NEWS REUTERS\par \par \uc2 Hungary risks driving off investors -business groups\par \par \uc2 Hungary's unorthodox economic policy is making its business environment unpredictable and eating into investors' confidence in the country, the American Chamber of Commerce and other multinational companies warned on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-Slight return of risk appetite lifts CEE assets The zloty and forint led emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher on Tuesday, benefiting from the return of some appetite for riskier assets and underpinned by the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region.\par \par \uc2 PREVIEW-Weak \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  growth seen keeping C/A in surplus\par \par \uc2 *WHAT: \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to publish Q2 current account figures\par \par \uc2 *WHEN: Sept 30, 0730\par \par \uc2 REUTERS FORECAST: The median forecast of analysts in a Aug 31-Sept 26 poll was for a current account surplus of 0.82 billion euros in the second quarter of the year.\par \par \uc2 HUNGARIAN PRESS\par \par \uc2 CABINET TO FINALISE DRAFT BUDGET TODAY The cabinet will finalise the draft 2012 budget today, prime ministerial spokesman Peter Szijjarto told reporters after the governing party MPs met on Tuesday. The budget, he said, will aim to advance the flat tax regime, close all tax loopholes, and put the pension and health insurance funds "back on their feet". The cabinet also aims to get at least 200,000 of the 595,000 people now drawing unemployment benefits back into the working world through the Start work programme.\par \par \uc2 TEACHERS TO JOIN UNION PROTEST\par \par \uc2 The Teachers Union will join Saturday's demonstration organised by four trade unions. Teachers will speak up for fair taxation, the restoration of social dialogue and for consultations with trade unions on a new career model.\par \par \uc2 (Hungarian press source: taken from Nepszabadsag's Hungary Around the Clock service. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Krisztina Than)\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY-FACTORS/   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110928e79s0008h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
