\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MONEY-Hungary cbank would love to cut but hands tied\b0\par\par\uc2 868 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2011\par 12:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Economy needs lower rates, market risks do not allow easing\par \par \uc2 * Hasty cut could dent bank's credibility if euro crisis deepens\par \par \uc2 * Bank must "warm up" markets before any cuts -analysts\par \par \uc2 By Sandor Peto\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, Sept 6 (Reuters) - Much has been made of the split between Hungary's government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the truth is that the bank would now love to cut interest rates to help the economy.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's move to weaken the franc on Tuesday may just conceivably have given them some room to do so - but not much and not in a rush.\par \par \uc2 Inflation is not an especially large problem in an economy that is almost static, but the heavy exposure of central Europe's most volatile emerging market to Swiss franc loans means the bank cannot afford to risk a forint sell-off.\par \par \uc2 Growth-smothering interest rates of six percent -- among the highest in Europe -- seem to be the cost the country now has to pay.\par \par \uc2 That arithmetic may have changed a little with the SNB's shock move, which knocked 8 percent off the franc's value to the euro, though most analysts say it could still take years before Hungary will have room to ease the cost of borrowing by a full percentage point or more.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk (for households' mortgage loans) has decreased with that (SNB move)," said Zsolt Kondrat, analyst at \uc2 MKB Bank\uc2  in Budapest.\par \par \uc2 "I see no rate cut in September, a small cut may come late this year, but the bank must (first) prepare the ground for it."\par \par \uc2 DOMESTIC SPLIT\par \par \uc2 When Prime Minister Viktor Orban appointed four new members to the seven-seat Monetary Council in March, investors expected the body's new majority to loosen policy this year to support the ruling Fidesz party's pro-growth agenda.\par \par \uc2 Growth stalled in the second quarter, prompting ministers to renew calls for lower rates as they pledged new tax hikes to help plug the resulting hole in budget revenues.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself is now likely to cut its growth and inflation forecasts in a quarterly report this month, something policymakers could normally follow with hints of lower rates.\par \par \uc2 But the euro zone debt crisis has spooked investors and those seeking safe havens for their cash, driving the franc higher versus the euro and closely-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the forint .\par \par \uc2 Even with the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  has little choice but to keep the premium for holding the forint high.\par \par \uc2 "The bank has no good options. It must choose the lesser evil," said Zsolt Papp, fund manager at UBP SA, which manages $1 billion in emerging fixed income assets.\par \par \uc2 "Cutting rates would be better but that's hard in an uncertain market environment."\par \par \uc2 Any falls for the forint mean higher monthly repayments for the tens of thousands of Hungarians who hold franc-denominated loans, and would further hurt already low domestic demand.\par \par \uc2 They would also raise pressure on Hungarian banks, which face rising non-performing loan rates. According to the financial market watchdog PSZAF, loans overdue more than 90 days accounted for 13.9 percent of all loans to households at the end of March.\par \par \uc2 The forint -- which traded at around 150 against the franc three years ago -- was bid around 228 on Tuesday, off from record lows at 271.62 four weeks ago, but much weaker than April's 200.\par \par \uc2 Hungary already leads its neighbours in terms of vulnerability, which the market expresses in the cost of insuring its debt. Five-year credit default swaps are now bid at 432 basis points, the highest level since April 2009 and much higher than Poland or the Czech Republic.\par \par \uc2 That means that a hasty rate cut now could later force the bank into a new hiking cycle if there is a serious spillover of euro zone market risks into Hungarian assets.\par \par \uc2 "WARMING UP" MARKETS\par \par \uc2 The weak growth figures and the proximity of the next inflation report have raised expectations of a cut in the past few weeks with interest rate swaps (IRS) now pricing in 25-50 basis points in cuts for the next couple of months.\par \par \uc2 That is still likely contingent on a calming of the euro zone crisis and/or the U.S. Federal Reserve launching new monetary stimulus. The bank may also wait to see whether the government's 2012 budget poses additional inflation pressures vis-\u224\'00\'E0-vis Orban's pledged tax hikes.\par \par \uc2 Barring extraordinary comments by policymakers, the next opportunity to prime market expectations for a shift to easing would be after the bank's next rate meeting on Sept. 20.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts argue, however, that a small cut may simply have no impact. Hendrik Scheerlink, CEO of KBC unit \uc2 K&H Bank\uc2 , says it is rather rising non-performing franc loans, an extraordinary banking tax, and the economic slowdown in European export markets that are crushing new credit.\par \par \uc2 "These factors are more relevant at the moment than the interest rates set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 192.151 Hungarian Forints)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Sandor Peto; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY-RATES (CEE MONEY)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110909e796000p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
