\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  recover on weak dollar, forint leads way\b0\par\par\uc2 908 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2011\par 16:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar weak as U.S. debt deadlock in focus\par \par \uc2 * Hungary cbank holds interest rates on hold at 6 percent\par \par \uc2 * Poland cbank says does not rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Luiza Ilie\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE/BUCHAREST, July 26 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint trimmed gains against the euro on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left interest rates flat, while other emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up their earlier gains.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept rates on hold at 6 percent\par \par \uc2 on Tuesday for the sixth month running to curb price growth to the bank's 3 percent inflation target.\par \par \uc2 By 1340 GMT, the forint had edged down to 267.96 to the euro, still up 0.3 percent on the day.\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown edged up 0.3 percent to near its 55-day moving average of 24.357 per euro. Poland's zloty\par \par \uc2 lost some steam and was hovering around the psychologically key 4.0 per euro level, up 0.1 percent on the day.\par \par \uc2 Stock markets in central Europe were weaker on the day across the region, led by Prague , which was off 1.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 Deadlock in talks in Washington over raising the debt limit to avoid a first-ever U.S. default has pushed investors away from the dollar, which fell broadly on Tuesday and lifted appetite for emerging European assets.\par \par \uc2 While markets last week gave a cautious welcome to a euro zone deal giving heavily indebted Greece easier borrowing terms and fresh aid, implementation risks remain and dealers said central Europe can still feel pressure from this.\par \par \uc2 But for now, focus has shifted to the one-week deadline to lift the U.S. debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 "Until the U.S. debt ceiling issue is clarified it will be very hard to see sustainable risk appetite in the region or elsewhere," one Bucharest-based trader said.\par \par \uc2 HAWKISH HUNGARIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Andras Simor said that in order to meet a 3 percent inflation target for 2012 "keeping interest rates at the current level may be necessary." He added that the euro zone debt crisis was the key risk for interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Investors were listening to Simor for hints on whether the bank will maintain a neutral monetary policy stance or signal an easing bias.\par \par \uc2 "The tone was a bit more hawkish than at the previous meeting, probably because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't afford a dovish tone at this point, which may put the HUF at risk of weakening," said Nordea's Elisabeth Andreew.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts were expecting a rate cut before the end of this year, with earlier expectations that the bank may raise rates -- after a 75 basis point tightening cycle that ended in January -- having evaporated.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the region, monetary tightening remains on the cards later this year in Poland and the Czech Republic. In Romania, where the key rate at 6.25 percent is higher than in Hungary, recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments have triggered some modest expectations of a rate cut.\par \par \uc2 Romania's leu added 0.6 percent to the euro, recovering after the government's failure to sell a minority stake in oil and gas giant \uc2 Petrom\uc2  last week tumbled shares in the unit.\par \par \uc2 Romania aims to push on with the sale of stakes in energy firms, the economy ministry said on Tuesday, despite the failed attempt to list \uc2 Petrom\uc2  shares on the bourse.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Marek Belka said he did not rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but only to limit volatility, not to defend a specific level of the zloty.\par \par \uc2 "It is no surprise that he says they are ready to do \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; he is the fourth or fifth management board guy to say this in the last 2.5 weeks," said Nomura's Peter Montalto.\par \par \uc2 "We think that means they'll strongly defend 4.1 and try and keep EURPLN around or below 4.0." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT-------------------- \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local \par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                            change   change \par                                            today    in 2011  \par Czech crown        24.329    24.401  +0.3%   +2.76% \par Polish zloty       4.003    4.005    +0.05%  -1.12% \par Hungarian forint   268.05    268.81  +0.28%  +3.7% \par Croatian kuna      7.448    7.443    -0.07%  -0.91% \par Romanian leu       4.23    4.255     +0.59%  +0.07% \par Serbian dinar      103.17    103.82  +0.63%  +2.67% \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yield Spreads Czech treasury bonds <0#CZBMK=> \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR    -2 basis points to  20bps over bmk* \par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR    -1 basis points to  +88bps over bmk* \par 10-yr T-bond   CZ9YT=RR    -4 basis points to  +102bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 