\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4-Leu rises on possible cbank move, forint slips\b0\par\par\uc2 969 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2011\par 17:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Bucharest dealers says c.bank likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Forint down half percent, sticks at lows after rates held\par \par \uc2 * Zloty dips on dovish cbank comments\par \par \uc2 (Adds suspected leu \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , more details)\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Dagmara Leszkowicz\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE/WARSAW, Feb 21 (Reuters) - The Romanian leu rose to a five-month high on Monday in what dealers said looked to be \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint held near session lows after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left interest rates on hold.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which never comments on market activities, was the first this year and helped the leu to buck a weakening trend in emerging Europe caused by falling risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 The region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under pressure from falling stock markets, a drop in the euro, spreading anti-government protests in Libya and the Middle East, and ongoing concern over euro zone peripheral Portugal's high budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 To counter this, Bucharest dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked like it stepped in the market indirectly through banks.\par \par \uc2 "We suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly sold euros through two local banks," said one dealer with a foreign bank in Bucharest.\par \par \uc2 Another dealer said volumes were twice those of a normal trading day.\par \par \uc2 "It seems they are afraid of inflationary pressures ... looming food inflation is a reality," the dealer said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers have said the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a tight band of around 4.1-4.3 per euro and the government frequently baulks at selling debt at high yields.\par \par \uc2 By 1551 GMT, the leu <EURRON=> added 0.3 percent to bid at 4.227 to the euro. The Czech crown <EURCZK=> was flat, while the forint <EURHUF=> fell 0.5 percent from Friday, but remained steady after the rate decision.\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY RATES\par \par \uc2 The Hungary \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as expected, kept interest rates unchanged at 6 percent in its last meeting before four new members join the Monetary Council, after a string of three-quarter point rate rises. [ID:nLDE71K1J6]\par \par \uc2 The bank said these rate increases would help inflation fall to its target as the direct impacts of cost-side shocks fade.\par \par \uc2 "That is no surprise to us -- or anybody else for that matter," said Lars Christensen, economist at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 . "With growth still lacklustre and inflation set to moderate there is really no reason for hiking rates at the moment."\par \par \uc2 Analysts have said board changes could lead to looser policy as appointments will be made by the centre-right Fidesz government which has openly criticised the bank for raising interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Bond yields remained unchanged after the decision. Forward rate markets still priced an additional hike in three months, but dealers have said this would likely be priced out if government reform plans, due to be unveiled next month, meet market expectations.\par \par \uc2 Hungary and Poland are the only two central European countries to have started raising interest rates, with the Czechs likely on hold in the coming months. Romania is expected to try to loosen policy to boost its economy.\par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty <EURPLN=> lost 0.6 percent to the euro on weakening market sentiment and comments of Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor that pointed to a more moderate pace of its own monetary policy tightening.\par \par \uc2 Markets have raised bets the Monetary Policy Council will follow a January rate rise from a record low with another hike at the council's March meeting. [ID:nLDE71K0GL]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head Marek Belka said on Monday it should act with moderation if there is no wage pressure and the January rise would not be followed by a "cascade" of further hikes.\par \par \uc2 "We're less confident now with a possible rate hike in March (after Belka's comments), but we also bear in mind that his comments are more ambiguous recently," said Rafal Benecki, senior economist at ING bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2011 \par Czech crown      <EURCZK=>   24.452   24.443  -0.04%   +2.24%\par Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>    3.938    3.915  -0.58%   +0.51%\par Hungarian forint <EURHUF=>  271.00   269.56   -0.53%   +2.58%\par Croatian kuna    <EURHRK=>    7.405    7.405   0%      -0.34%\par Romanian leu     <EURRON=>    4.227    4.24   +0.31%   +0.14%\par Serbian dinar    <EURRSD=>  103.15   103.1    -0.05%   +2.69%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds <0#CZBMK=>\par 2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR   +3 basis points to  37bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR   +4 basis points to  +84bps over bmk*\par 1