\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks hit 2-wk high, forint recovers\b0\par\par\uc2 486 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2010\par 13:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Emerging stocks rise nearly 1 pct, spreads tighten\par \par \uc2 * Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally, forint up after c.bank comments\par \par \uc2 * Lithuania sounding investors out for Eurobond\par \par \uc2 By Carolyn Cohn\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 2 (Reuters) - Emerging stocks hit two-week highs and several emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose 1 percent on Thursday, boosted by strong U.S. and Chinese data, and the Hungarian forint recovered after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments. Wall Street posted its best day in eight weeks on Wednesday following higher than anticipated U.S. and Chinese purchasing managers' data.\par \par \uc2 That renewed investor appetite for riskier assets following a 2 percent loss in emerging stocks last month.\par \par \uc2 "Investors were positioned for more bearish news and changed tack when Chinese PMI and U.S. ISM figures came out better than expected," said Kasper Bartholdy, head of sovereign strategy and co-head of economics at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The numbers are no cause for jubilation but they are not as disastrous as some people thought." The MSCI emerging equities index <.MSCIEF> rose half a percent to two-week highs and the Thomson Reuters emerging equity index <.TRXFLDEEPU> gained 0.2 percent.\par \par \uc2 Emerging sovereign debt spreads <11EMJ> tightened 2 basis points to 286 bps after narrowing sharply on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Investors expect fresh emerging debt supply over the next few months.\par \par \uc2 Lithuania has sounded investors out over a seven-year euro-denominated bond, that would raise at least 500 million euros, during a roadshow this week, fund managers said. [ID:nLDE6801QJ]\par \par \uc2 FORINT RECOVERS\par \par \uc2 Most emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting later on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The forint climbed nearly 1 percent against the euro <EURHUF=> and held above record lows against the Swiss franc <CHFHUF=> after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Andras Simon told Reuters on Wednesday that the strong Swiss franc posed risks to Hungary's economy, comments which \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  described in a client note as "quasi-verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 Simon also said \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  may need the support of an IMF and European Union safety net if global investor sentiment turns negative.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's talks with the IMF and EU about a review of its current financing deal collapsed in July. This deal, which it took to fend off a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis in October 2008, runs out next month.\par \par \uc2 Reflecting the continued nervousness, Hungary sold 15 billion forints less than its original offer in a 12-month T-bill auction on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "We recommend using the current rally to rebuild long EURHUF or PLNHUF positions," said \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  analysts in a client note.\par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty <EURPLN=> and South African rand <ZAR=> also rose at least 1 percent, but the Romanian leu hit fresh five-week lows <EURRON=> as investors fret about political will to implement austerity measures.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Sujata Rao and Sebastian Tong; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|HX|PX|CZS|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100905e6920005p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
