\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary Central Bank \highlight\uc2  To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  At EUR/HUF 290\b0\par\par\uc2 1,314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2010\par 11:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0914 GMT [Dow Jones] If the EUR/HUF rate moves above 290 this week, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect the HUF, Nomura says. Should EUR/HUF rise above 310-315, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to raise interest rates from the current 5.25%, Nomura adds. The IMF/EU left Hungary earlier than planned and without a deal Saturday. EUR/HUF is 288.72 from 289.03 early morning. Nomura warns that a CHF rally vs the HUF means a "double whammy" for Hungarian households, which mostly have CHF-based debt. Adds a crisis could be good for Hungary on the long run, "bringing politicians back to the straight and narrow." Recommends staying short in Hungarian assets. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0913 GMT [Dow Jones] India interest rate swaps see slight receiving interest across curve, reflecting lower government bond yields, says dealer with private bank. Adds, swaps falling on signs of liquidity trickling back into banking system, while bond yields fall as no federal government debt sale scheduled this week. 1-year OIS rate at 5.75%/5.79% vs 5.77%/5.81% last close, 5-year OIS rate at 6.81%/6.85% vs 6.83%/6.86% last close. "A rate hike at RBI's policy meeting (on July 27) is already priced in and swaps will likely move in a tight range," dealer says. Tips 1-year OIS in 5.70%-5.85% range, 5-year OIS in 6.78%/6.88% range till RBI policy meeting. RBI Friday decided to extend second daily liquidity auction facility till July 30 to help banks manage liquidity better. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0907 GMT [Dow Jones] KLCI ends down 0.3% at 1333.35, in line with weaker regional bourses. "The profit taking is not a surpise but trading volume is healthy, and the index staying above 1326 (10-day moving average) gives it a good base to rise further this week," says dealer. Maybank IB Research says chart signals still positive with KLCI having potential to test 1349 in coming weeks. Market breadth turns marginally positive late with advancers beating decliners 327 to 319. Among actives, Titan (5103.KU) +18.4% at MYR2.19, Time (4456.KU) +4.4% at MYR0.475, Scomi (7158.KU) +3.7% at MYR0.425, UEM Land (5148.KU) +3.8% at MYR1.62, JCY (5161.KU) down 2.0% at MYR1.48, Berjaya Corp (3395.KU) down 1.7% at MYR1.14. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0901 GMT [Dow Jones] China onshore IRS down, tracking lower U.S. Treasury yields after weaker-than-expected U.S. consumer-sentiment report Friday. 1-year down 3 bps at 2.03%-2.13%, 5-year down 6 bps at 2.72%-2.82%, 1-to-5-year spread 3 bps narrower at 71 bps. Shanghai-based local bank trader says swaps can fall more as concerns over strength in U.S. economic recovery persist. "If the U.S. economy is facing a double-dip (recession), China's market will also suffer." China PBOC Vice Gov. Du Jinfu says inflation pressures have eased in China, also weighing on rates. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0851 GMT [Dow Jones] The dollar is mixed nudging slightly higher against the JPY as equities recover from a shaky start and risk appetite returns. The pound is a little firmer for much the same reason although the big mover of the session has been the euro which has bounced sharply from its lows seen after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  one notch downgrade of Ireland. The euro is up at $1.2970, the pound is up at 1.5317 and the dollar is up at Y86.91. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0848 GMT [Dow Jones] Greece/10-year bund spread on Monday rises to 780bps, up 20bps from the open on international uncertainty. Turnover of the local HDAT and European trading platform is moderate at EUR6M. "The fact that talks between Hungary and the EU/IMF have stalled and Ireland was downgraded is adding pressure to euro zone periphery spreads," says a senior local trader. "I expect spreads to widen to about 800bps this week due to a lack of interest given the summer holiday mood." (nick.skrekas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0847 GMT [Dow Jones] September bunds slip and are flat on the day as equity markets pare initial losses. The market had got a bid in initial trading after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgraded Ireland but risk aversion seems to be abating. "We've seen some amount of profit taking and the euro also seems to be holding up pretty well against the Yen so that's also dragged on safe havens," says Kenneth Broux at \uc2 Lloyds TSB\uc2 . He says the market may continue to trade in a narrow range until Fed Chairman Bernanke's testimony on Wednesday, while the bank stress results on Friday will also be eyed. September bunds unchanged at 129.16 vs 129.54 session high. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0847 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan average interbank overnight rate lower at 0.192% vs 0.195% Friday. Trader says \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants government-controlled banks to borrow less from call market today. "Liquidity is not so tight today," she says. Thinks overnight rate biased up in near term as government-controlled banks likely to set offering rate higher but "the market liquidity will likely remain ample if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raises the rate gradually," she says. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  guides government-controlled banks to set rate at 0.190% since Thursday vs 0.189% Wednesday. (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0846 GMT [Dow Jones]USD/IDR late higher at 9,065 vs 9,050 Friday, but off intraday high of 9,071, tracking greenback's strength against Asia's major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say. "We expect the pair will hover around this level tomorrow," dealer says; tips range of 9,040-9,080 Tuesday. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0842 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/SEK called to head higher toward 9.55/9.77 before going down again, says Nordea, noting Friday's session saw the krona weaken to 9.4950 from 9.4300 as profit-taking in risk took place. "The market will be looking to buy on dips towards 9.47/9.48. The expected range today is 9.4900-9.5600," Nordea says. EUR/SEK trades at 9.5239.(ian.edmondson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0840 GMT [Dow Jones] BP shares -2.9% to 395p, after US authorities expressed concerns that hydrocarbons could seep from the newly sealed Macondo oil well. "BP seems to have hit another road bump so that's not going to do the space any favors," says one trader. Another says there is also some trepidation ahead of the 2Q results, July 27. \uc2 UBS\uc2  says while underlying earnings and cashflows are expected to be good, accounting for the spill is likely to be complex. "The release should allow for a much needed insight into the balance sheet...its liquidity resources and the commitments it faces. The relief well is critical in defining these commitments." (andrea.tryphonides@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0838 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR higher despite rising EUR as demand from oil companies, NDF players support, says trader with private bank. Pair last at 47.02 vs 46.78 late Friday. "You can see Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are underperforming against the dollar. But some importer and NDF buying is hurting the rupee," trader says. Adds, unwinding of long-EUR/Asia positions in NDF market also driving pair higher. Trader tips key resistance at 47.10, 46.60-47.35 band this week. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com) [ 07-19-10 0514ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100719e67j0005z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
