 like the koruna will trade in a range from 25.650 to 25.800, there doesn't seem to be much push for the koruna to stay at firmer levels below 25.700," Roman Fol, a Raiffeisenbank trader, says. The EUR/CZK is driven by the overall sentiment on other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region. "There's some waiting on what'll happen elsewhere," Fol says. (leos.rousek@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0929 GMT [Dow Jones] The forint weakens against the euro as western European markets trade in the red, but HUF remains in the range seen for the past week, a trader says. EUR/HUF is at 281.10 versus 280.50 Wednesday afternoon, but the 278-282 range is likely to hold, Takarekbank says. USD/HUF is at 228.53 but the 225-230 range is unlikely to break, Takarekbank says. CHF/HUF is watched as CHF has been rallying since SNB signaled it would soften \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , negative news for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's large number of borrowers using CHF. CHF/HUF is at 207.58 and the next important levels are seen between 208-209, Takarekbank adds. CHF/HUF closed at 205.46 Wednesday. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0928 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR forward premia under pressure on view that spot gains may draw selling interest from firms looking to exit USD holdings now, says trader with foreign bank; 1-year forward premium at 1.32 vs 1.355 late Wednesday. Notes upward pressure on forwards in recent sessions stemming from concerns near-term interest rates may rise may also have been overdone, leaving forward premia vulnerable to correction. Still for today, major correction not on cards as spot move up largely driven by buying from large private engineering firm, capping of spot at current levels may ease downward pressure on premia.(bijou.george@dowjones.com) [ 06-24-10 0622ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100624e66o0007j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw