\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  If EUR/HUF Hits 290\b0\par\par\uc2 1,306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2010\par 11:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0936 GMT [Dow Jones] Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unlikely to tolerate EUR/HUF trading above 290 and will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the pair rises above that rate, predicts Takarekbank. HUF plunged Friday, hitting 290, after government officials made comments on Hungary's economic situation. HUF earlier Monday retraced some of the weakness but is now again weaker at 288.0 from 285.9 in the morning. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0936 GMT [Dow Jones] The Swedish social democratic opposition party wants the EU's stability pact to be tightened, and says that countries that violate the pact ought not to receive EU funding, says SEB. Adds: "The idea of cutting EU funding to countries that misbehave is interesting. Above all, it would exert pressure on governments to stick to the rules in order not to risk public protest when no EU money is received." EUR/SEK trades at 9.6504. (karl.bruze@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0932 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR pares earlier gains, last at 9,265, off 9,300 intraday high after Bank Indonesia suspected of selling $50 million at near 9,300 earlier in day. But pair still above 9,190 late Friday, as falls in major stock markets, fresh worries over euro zone's debt problems help strengthen dollar against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; "those sentiments will still be there tomorrow, but (the pair) will likely be less volatile," dealer says; 9,250-9,300 tipped for Tuesday.(andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0928 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai government bonds higher in thin trade as disappointing U.S. jobs data Friday, heightened worries after Hungary added to euro-zone sovereign debt woes stoke demand in safe haven assets. Benchmark 9-year yield briefly dips to 3.14% today, unseen level this year, says bond dealer; adds offshore players seen buying. "Stock markets in Europe and the U.S. will dictate yields of (Thai) government bonds tomorrow. Yields may fall up to 4 basis points if both bourses slide sharply," says dealer. Bid/offer yields of issue due May 2015 quoted at 3.02%/3.00% vs 3.08%/3.05% late Friday, November 2016 at 3.15%/3.12% vs 3.23%/3.18%, June 2019 3.17%/3.13% vs 3.30%/3.25%. (oranan.paweewun@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0928 GMT [Dow Jones] Greece/10-year bund spread widens to 570 bps from an open of 555 bps, amid very thin volume of only EUR4M on the local HDAT platform. "Greek spreads are widening along with all other euro zone countries and naturally the significant weakness of the common European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't help," says a trader. "I see no signs for this widening to reverse itself especially since there is so little buying interest," he adds. (nskrekas@trk.forthnet.gr)\par \par \uc2 0926 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysian shares end lower, benchmark KLCI down 0.6% at 1286.27 in lackluster volume; dealer says market jittery on fresh concerns over euro zone debt problems, some staying on sidelines in absence of fresh leads. "Sentiment remains bearish, we think investors are taking a very short-term view so any rebound is unlikely to last," says dealer; tips immediate support at 1270, resistance at 1300. Decliners trounce advancers; decliners include AirAsia (5099.KU) down 4.6% at MYR1.26, Maybank (1155.KU) down 1.0% at MYR7.31, Proton (5304.KU) down 3.8% at MYR4.55. Gamuda (5398.KU) bucks market, +1.0% at MYR2.99. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0924 GMT [Dow Jones] China onshore IRS lower on looser liquidity conditions as subscriptions for Bank of China's (601988.SH) CNY40 billion convertible bond expire lock-up period today. 1-year down 2 bps at 2.18%-2.25%, 5-year down 7 bps at 3.02%-3.10%, 1-to-5-year spread 5 bps lower at 84 bps. "Downside in the short-term swaps is really limited as more banks' fund-raising plans are on the way," says Shanghai-based local bank trader. Agricultural Bank of China plans to sell 58.4 billion shares in Shanghai, Hong Kong IPO, while Bank of Communications plans to raise CNY33.1 billion from rights issue in 2 markets. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0923 GMT [Dow Jones] Credit Agricole CIB expects Spain to launch its new 2.50% October 2013-dated bond Thursday with an issuance size of "anything up to EUR4 billion," but as the 2013 bucket is already a heavily tapped part of the Spanish curve, absorption of this bond "will not be easy and will likely to continue to weigh post auction." The bank's analysts say the 2-3-year segment of the Spanish curve seems to be under the most pressure at the moment as the market makes room for this bond. The Treasury will announce the target volume for the auction later Monday. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0922 GMT [Dow Jones] Taiwan's May exports +57.9% on year vs April +47.8% with record high value on strong demand from Asia as global economy recovers, says \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . CPI +0.74% on year in May vs April +1.34% on moderating fuel costs, according to statistics agency. Latest trade, inflation data unlikely to spur rate hikes by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at policy meeting on June 24 given rising downside risks on pace of recovery in 2H, says \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  economist Cheng Cheng-mount. If left unsolved, "Europe's debt problems may start to slow demand for the island's electronic products in the fourth quarter," he says. (crystal.hsu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0920 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CZK trades lower at 25.810-25.860 from 25.870 late Friday as Czech data Monday shows the export-oriented country is ramping up industrial production and maintaining a solid trade surplus, together lifting the koruna. EUR/CZK downward moves are going to be limited later today, however, by concerns in the region that optimism could be misplaced as debt concerns remain in Hungary and in Czech trading partners in the eurozone, traders say. (sean.carney@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0912 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  recommends buying long HUF positions as expects Hungary to reach the official 3.8% of GDP budget deficit in 2010. Hungarian assets plunged after government officials' remarks on the severe state of the Hungarian economy. "We now need to see concrete policy steps to meet the International Monetary Fund and EU [budget shortfall] targets regardless of what the initial state of the economy is," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  says. Says the series of events will teach the new government that economic policy is a serious matter and that markets are "fickle and unforgivable to policy or communication mistakes." (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0912 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares end down 2.6% at 2750.233 in light volume, off intraday low of 2702.069, weighed by falls across Asian markets amid worries that sovereign debt problems in Europe could slow global economic recovery, traders say. "Bargain buying mostly by local institutional funds lifted the main index from its low amid a generally weak sentiment," says fund manager at state-owned pension fund; expects shares to rebound tomorrow on more buying at low levels; tips resistance at 2800. Among decliners: tin producer Timah (TINS.JK) down 6.6% at IDR2,125 as tin prices fall 8.6% on Kuala Lumpur market, car maker Astra (ASII.JK) down 2.6% at IDR43,500, rebounding from IDR41,950 intraday low, Bank Rakyat (BBRI.JK) down 2.3% at IDR8,550, but off IDR8,300 low. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com) [ 06-07-10 0536ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100607e6670006z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
