\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-Assets fall on risk aversion, Romania hit hard\b0\par\par\uc2 1,019 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2010\par 18:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stocks, bonds fall on renewed euro zone worries\par \par \uc2 * Romanian stocks nosedive 11 pct on strike concerns\par \par \uc2 * Polish cbank keeps rates on hold\par \par \uc2 (Recasts with new prices, comments)\par \par \uc2 By Dagmara Leszkowicz and Sandor Peto\par \par \uc2 WARSAW/BUDAPEST, May 25 (Reuters) - Central European assets fell on Tuesday as risk aversion grew globally and markets in the neighbouring euro zone got an additional hit from fears that the debt crisis in its southern peripheries was widening.\par \par \uc2 Romania's stock index <.BETI> was worst hit, plunging 11 percent due to concern about looming strikes against drastic budget cuts agreed with the IMF. [ID:nLDE64O13K]\par \par \uc2 Central Europe's reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro <EUR=>, touched a four-year trough against the dollar after Spain's weekend takeover of a small savings bank and political tension on the Korean peninsula added to global risk aversion. [ID:nN25121933]\par \par \uc2 The region's main equity indices, excluding Romania, fell 2.4-5.2 percent to about three-month lows.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Bulgarian credit default swaps rose 25 basis points to 280 as the country said its budget deficit could be 4.8 percent of gross domestic product in 2010, far above initial estimates. [ID:nLDE64O0KP]\par \par \uc2 While the strong presence of Greek banks make Romania and Bulgaria more vulnerable to the euro zone crisis than other emerging economies in the European Union, deficit and debt levels in central Europe are healthier than in many euro zone countries.\par \par \uc2 However, the region is heavily reliant on exports to western Europe, and its assets are vulnerable to risk aversion.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses were led by the region's most liquid unit, the zloty <EURPLN=>, which fell 1.7 percent against the euro by 1502 GMT. Hungary's forint <EURHUF=> shed 0.9 percent, while the Czech crown <EURCZK=> was down 0.4 percent and Romania's leu <EURRON=> dipped 0.2 percent.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said nervousness over Romania's political situation was better reflected in stocks as the leu may be protected by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it weakens markedly.\par \par \uc2 Serbia's dinar <EURRSD=> hit record lows and it was bid at 102.51, slightly off lows at 103.37. Serbia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold 856.5 million euros this year to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including its latest 20 million euro sale on Monday.[ID:nLDE64O0QN]\par \par \uc2 POLAND HOLDS RATES\par \par \uc2 Hungarian government bond yield spreads over corresponding Bund yields rose 19-26 basis points, Polish yields rose 13-18 basis points, while Czech yields rose 10-14 basis points. Bond prices at the long end of the curve suffered mostly.\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its key interest rate <PLINTR=ECI> on hold at a record low 3.5 percent. It said inflation was likely to ease in coming months. [ID:nLDE64N11C]\par \par \uc2 The bank's statement had little comment on the zloty's retreat after strong gains earlier this year, although the minutes of the bank's April meeting showed that rate setters paid significant attention to the zloty.\par \par \uc2 Rate setter Jan Wijniecki said the weakening zloty was beneficial to the economy. [ID:nLDE64N11C]\par \par \uc2 Some Budapest-based dealers said central banks in the region might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market if the current turmoil continues. \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  never comments on market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and dealers said the bank was unlikely to cut rates further at a meeting on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Current forint levels against the euro and the Swiss franc are already painful to Hungarian households who hold a large amount of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans.\par \par \uc2 "Even without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market players have become very cautious (in the region)," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. "There have been big swings in both directions and many people have burnt themselves."\par \par \uc2 "If there are even bigger falls in developed equity markets, let's say about 10 percent, the forint may try to settle in weaker territories at 285-290 (from around 280)," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2010 \par  Czech crown      <EURCZK=>   25.638   25.526   -0.44%    +2.65%\par  Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>    4.169    4.099   -1.68%    -1.56%\par  Hungarian forint <EURHUF=>  280.14   277.67    -0.88%    -3.49%\par  Croatian kuna    <EURHRK=>    7.27     7.269   -0.01%    +0.54%\par  Romanian leu     <EURRON=>    4.183    4.175   -0.19%    +1.3%\par  Serbian dinar    <EURRSD=>  102.51   102.41    -0.1%     -6.47%\par  Yield Spreads\par  Czech treasury bonds <0#CZBMK=>\par  2-yr T-bond   CZ2YT=RR   +10 basis points to  134bps over bmk*\par  7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR   +14 basis points to  +150bps over bm