\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE: Hungary MPC: Further Rate Cuts Hinge On Risk Assessment\b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2010\par 16:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds comment from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor.)\par \par \uc2 By Margit Feher and Veronika Gulyas\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--Interest rates, rather than direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forint market, will remain the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main policy tool and further rate cuts will continue to hinge on investors' risk perception of the country, National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Andras Simor said Monday.\par \par \uc2 Following direct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Poland and in light of the recent, relative strength of the forint, expectations have been growing that the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also use direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main policy tool is its rate policy, but we don't exclude direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from our policy tools," Simor said.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no exchange rate target, Simor reiterated. However, "there are such exchange rate levels which are detrimental to the economy and pose a risk to the country's financial stability," Simor said when asked to reveal conditions under which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forint market.\par \par \uc2 Simor also said there could be sharp or sudden volatile forint movements which the corporate sector couldn't accommodate, which could also serve as a reason for direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Simor was speaking at a press conference after the bank's monetary policy council decided in a vote with a decisive majority to cut the policy rate by 0.25 percentage point rather than by 0.50 percentage point, the other option it discussed.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation and the real economy outlook would justify further rate cuts, which could take place if Hungary's risk perception (among investors) makes that possible," the MPC said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The MPC Monday cut the policy rate for the tenth month in a row, to another record low of 5.25% from 5.50%.\par \par \uc2 "There's reason that would justify tighter monetary conditions. The economy has only been recovering slowly and the inflation outlook also shows that inflation will dip below the target--those would justify not a tightening but a loosening of the conditions," Simor added.\par \par \uc2 The MPC maintained that inflation will slow this year close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 3% inflation target and dip below that level next year, Simor added.\par \par \uc2 He noted, however, that worries persist on financial markets over Greece's debt situation.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mnb.hu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.mnb.hu}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Margit Feher and Veronika Gulyas, Dow Jones Newswires; +36-20-433-2074; veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 26, 2010 10:01 ET (14:01 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100426e64q003m2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
