\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-Forint holds post-election gains after cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2010\par 15:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Forint holds post-election gains after cbank cut\par \par \uc2  * Stocks throw support behind other \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Greece, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worries weigh\par \par \uc2  (Updates \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  cbank, prices)\par \par \uc2  By Dagmara Leszkowicz and Jason Hovet\par \par \uc2  WARSAW/PRAGUE, April 26 (Reuters) - A landslide Hungarian election victory for the centre-right Fidesz party gave a lift to the country's forint and bonds on Monday, as rising stock markets added support to other central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The forint touched its highest level in eight sessions after the Sunday run-off vote that gave Fidesz a clear two-thirds majority in parliament, and was unshaken later on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates to a new record low of 5.25 percent as expected. [ID:nLDE63P1FR]\par \par \uc2  "What happens next is a question of monetary policy as well as politics," Raiffeisen Bank analyst Zoltan Torok. \par \par \uc2  "I do not believe this was the last rate cut. There will be at least one more. We think it will come in the third quarter, but the outlook is very uncertain on that horizon."\par \par \uc2  The forint <EURHUF=> added 0.1 percent over Friday's close, bid at 263.1 to the euro by 1412 GMT. Bond yields held around multi-year lows hit this month.\par \par \uc2  Analysts expected a post-election bounce for Hungarian assets after Fidesz won the majority needed to launch vital reforms to get the economy back in gear after the country was near financial collapse two years ago. \par \par \uc2  But they said the grace period could be short and the new government's relationship with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be tense. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par   * For more stories on the Hungarian election, double-click\par [ID:nLDE63L1O6]\par   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2  The Budapest bourse <.BUX> also reach a 1-1/2 week high,\par rising 2.4 percent with global peers on an improving outlook for\par the United States, the world's biggest economy. [ID:nLDE63P0CZ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The rise in stocks mostly supported central Europe's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The Polish zloty <EURPLN=> and Romanian leu\par <EURRON=> rose 0.2 percent and 0.3 percent, while the Czech\par crown <EURCZK=> underperformed and was flat on the day. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Persistent uncertainty over aid for debt-laden Greece also\par knocked the euro, weighing on this region. [ID:nLDE63P0LU]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Greek 5-year credit default swaps (CDS) rose to records\par above 600 basis points on Monday. By comparison, Poland's 5-year\par CDS stood at around 105 bps, while Hungary's was at 187 basis\par points on Monday. [ID:nLDE63P0NZ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Dealers said investors have also become wary of possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in markets. Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised markets\par earlier this month with its first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 10 years to\par temper the surging zloty's impact on exports and the economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Emerging EU's better growth outlook and lower debt positions\par compared to the euro zone periphery states like Greece have\par turned investors' focus to the region more often, putting\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , bond and stocks to multi-month highs this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  In the past 12 months, the zloty has led \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with a\par 15 percent gain, compared to 12 percent for the forint, a 5 rise\par in the crown and 3 percent for the leu.\par  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2010 \par Czech crown      <EURCZK=>   25.387   25.392  +0.02%   +3.67%\par Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>    3.877    3.883  +0.15%   +5.86%\par Hungarian forint <EURHUF=>  263.13   263.5    +0.14%   +2.74%\par Croatian kuna    <EURHRK=>    7.256    7.255  -0.01%   +0.73%\par Romanian leu     <EURRON=>    4.11     4.123  +0.32%   +3.1%\par Serbian dinar    <EURRSD=>   99.18    99.043  -0.14%   -3.33%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds <0#CZBMK=>\par 3-yr T-bond   CZ3YT=RR   +2 basis points to  54bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR   +5 basis points to  +66bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ10YT=RR    -2 basis points to  +63bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All data taken from Reuters at 1513 CET.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  percent change calculated from the daily domestic \par close at 1600 GMT.\par For related news and prices, click on the codes in brackets: All\par emerging market news [EMRG] \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates Eastern Europe spot \f28