\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Hungary Deficit Target Could Rise To 5.5% Of GDP\b0\par\par\uc2 1,054 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2010\par 17:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1539 GMT [Dow Jones] Saxo Bank expects the opposition party Fidesz, which is slated to form the next government, to increase the 2010 fiscal deficit target to 5.5%-of-GDP from the prior 3.8%-of-GDP target. Saxo says this is likely to be due to losses made by state-owned companies. Fidesz has said the deficit for 2010 could rise to as high as 7.0%-7.5% of GDP. (melinda.szilagyi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1535 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Standard Chartered PLC\uc2  (A3/A) launched its $2B 5-year notes at 135 BP/Tsys, 10 bps narrow of prelimnary price guidance. The issue is expected to be priced in the private placement Rule 144a market via joint lead managers \uc2 Barclays\uc2 /CA/JPM/Scotia. (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1534 GMT [Dow Jones] Curve flatteners lift Jun 30-yr Tsy bond futures price to nearly 1-month high of 117-19. That's not far from resistance at 117-22, a move that reduces 30-yr cash yield equivalent to 4.625%, says Optima Investment Research. Jun 10-yr Tsy notes rise intraday price top of 117-02. Optima says further upside to 117-06 drops 10-yr cash yield equivalent to 3.75%. Resistance also at Mon's nearly 1-month high of 117-13+. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1518 GMT [Dow Jones] Longer-term Tsys outperforming as investors continue to put on curve flattening trades in absence of key data and Fed remarks, selling short-term Tsys and buying long-term ones. 2-yr down 1/32 to 1.028%, 10-yr up 11/32 to 3.757% and 30-yr up 27/32 to 4.621%. 2s/10s curve at 273 bps from 279 bps Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 (deborah.blumberg@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1446 GMT [Dow Jones] Emerging-market bond prices softer after posting modest gains in the previous trading session. Risk premium on \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's Emerging Market Bond Index Global widens 1bp to 249bps over Treasurys; index off 0.03%. Most country components of the benchmark Embig are flat though Ukraine and Uruguay both continue facing selling pressure for the second straight day. Brazilian debt unmoved with local markets closed for a holiday. (kejal.vyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1441 GMT [Dow Jones] There are plenty of deals in the European high-yield pipeline despite little action Wednesday, according to fund managers in London. Spanish telecoms operator ONO is slated to bring a new bond after the company recently recieved approval from banks for its refinancing plan. UK petrochemical company Ineos is also expected to bring a new deal as part of its EUR1 billion refinancing providing that the company's plan to amend its debt terms is passed. \uc2 Continental AG\uc2  (CON.XE) has also said it plans to bring a bond in the near future. (michael.wilson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1436 GMT [Dow Jones] CIB forecasts temporary HUF weakness against EUR due to political risks in wake of the general elections. However CIB says EUR/HUF could rise above 270 any time, should global sentiment sour again. EUR/HUF is at 263.40. CIB adds that the large EUR/HUF swings seen in March 2009 and October 2008 are unlikely to be repeated. It sees a chance of further rate cuts given improved market sentiment and relative HUF strength. Despite uncertainty over economic policy by the next government, it's likely to urge adoption of the euro. (melinda.szilagyi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1427 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be tempted into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by Poland's recent example, but that risk is minimal, says \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 . It notes the majority of Hungary's Monetary Policy Council wants to continue its easing cycle through cutting interest rates in 25bp clips a month and the MPC wouldn't want to add to HUF volatility by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly. Citi notes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last in 2009 by selling EUR/HUF. It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the early 2000s when it defended the bottom of the official EUR/HUF trading band. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1424 GMT [Dow Jones] Tokyo-based leasing and financing company \uc2 ORIX Corporation\uc2  (A3/A-) launched its $750M 5-year offering of SEC registered senior unsecured fixed-rate notes at Tsys +220 bps, directly in line with preliminary price guidance. Deal expected to be priced later Weds. via joint bookrunners BofAML/MS/\uc2 UBS\uc2 . (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1413 GMT [Dow Jones] Rexnord and its parent company RBS Global are in the market with $1.145 bln in senior notes due 2018. Proceeds will fund tender offers for the company's 9.5% sr unsecured notes due 2014 and 8.875% sr unsec notes due 2016.\par \par \uc2 (michael.aneiro@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1413 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are lower after the double whammy of hawkish BOE minutes and a bigger than forecast drop in UK jobless data. The BOE minutes show some members were concerned about rises in CPI and the number of people claiming unemployment benefit in the UK came in 32,900 lower for March vs expectations of a 15,000 drop. The DMO Thursday auctions GBP3.75 billion of UKT 4.75% 2020 after selling GBP600 million of 2017 linkers Wednesday. In data Thursday brings retail sales and public sector finances. 2-year/10-year gilt yield curve flattens to 307.8bps vs 308.6bps Tuesday. June gilts are down 9bps at 114.01 and the benchmark 10-year is down at 97.87 to yield 4.024%, within a 3.991%-4.044% range.(neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1403 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD is in a downtrend, says \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 , but investors shouldn't look for it to break much lower. The bank says EUR/USD is likely to adjust a little lower from the current $1.3406 level, but suggests the downside potential is not as deep as is generally perceived in the market. "We think that a third attempt to send EUR/USD below $1.33 will fail, making a bottom-fishing spot strategy attractive," says Danske. (peter.nurse@dowjones.com) [ 04-21-10 1139ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100421e64l000b3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
