\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: HUF To Ease Short-term, Firm Long-term - CIB\b0\par\par\uc2 1,179 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2010\par 16:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1436 GMT [Dow Jones] CIB forecasts temporary HUF weakness against EUR due to political risks in wake of the general elections. However CIB says EUR/HUF could rise above 270 any time, should global sentiment sour again. EUR/HUF is at 263.40. CIB adds that the large EUR/HUF swings seen in March 2009 and October 2008 are unlikely to be repeated. It sees a chance of further rate cuts given improved market sentiment and relative HUF strength. Despite uncertainty over economic policy by the next government, it's likely to urge adoption of the euro. (melinda.szilagyi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1427 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be tempted into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by Poland's recent example, but that risk is minimal, says \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 . It notes the majority of Hungary's Monetary Policy Council wants to continue its easing cycle through cutting interest rates in 25bp clips a month and the MPC wouldn't want to add to HUF volatility by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly. Citi notes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last in 2009 by selling EUR/HUF. It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the early 2000s when it defended the bottom of the official EUR/HUF trading band. (margit.feher@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1424 GMT [Dow Jones] Tokyo-based leasing and financing company \uc2 ORIX Corporation\uc2  (A3/A-) launched its $750M 5-year offering of SEC registered senior unsecured fixed-rate notes at Tsys +220 bps, directly in line with preliminary price guidance. Deal expected to be priced later Weds. via joint bookrunners BofAML/MS/\uc2 UBS\uc2 . (kellie.geressy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1413 GMT [Dow Jones] Rexnord and its parent company RBS Global are in the market with $1.145 bln in senior notes due 2018. Proceeds will fund tender offers for the company's 9.5% sr unsecured notes due 2014 and 8.875% sr unsec notes due 2016.\par \par \uc2 (michael.aneiro@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1413 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are lower after the double whammy of hawkish BOE minutes and a bigger than forecast drop in UK jobless data. The BOE minutes show some members were concerned about rises in CPI and the number of people claiming unemployment benefit in the UK came in 32,900 lower for March vs expectations of a 15,000 drop. The DMO Thursday auctions GBP3.75 billion of UKT 4.75% 2020 after selling GBP600 million of 2017 linkers Wednesday. In data Thursday brings retail sales and public sector finances. 2-year/10-year gilt yield curve flattens to 307.8bps vs 308.6bps Tuesday. June gilts are down 9bps at 114.01 and the benchmark 10-year is down at 97.87 to yield 4.024%, within a 3.991%-4.044% range.(neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1403 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD is in a downtrend, says \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 , but investors shouldn't look for it to break much lower. The bank says EUR/USD is likely to adjust a little lower from the current $1.3406 level, but suggests the downside potential is not as deep as is generally perceived in the market. "We think that a third attempt to send EUR/USD below $1.33 will fail, making a bottom-fishing spot strategy attractive," says Danske. (peter.nurse@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1400 GMT [Dow Jones] The IMF upgraded Canada's 2010 growth forecast to 3.1% from 2.6%, still slower than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest projection, and cut the 2011 view to 3.2% from 3.6%. The forecasts come a day after the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  raised its 2010 projection to 3.7% from 2.9% and lowered the figure for 2011 to 3.1% from 3.5%. The IMF said Canada's recovery would be "protracted," because of the strong Canadian dollar and more moderate demand growth than in the U.S. The Canadian economy shrank 2.6% last year. (nirmala.menon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1359 GMT [Dow Jones] The widening in Greek yield spreads might exaggerate the threat to EUR, says CitiFX. They are highlighting lingering market fears on a potential breakdown in the aid program before funds can be disbursed, it says. "However, the move appears exaggerated relative to other indicators of sentiment. On balance, we prefer positioning for a further decline in volatility to trading the back and forth in news flow in spot," CitiFX says. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1344 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds higher as investors remain concerned over Greek finances, with the yield spread between Greek bonds and bunds still fairly high. Marc Ostwald at Monument Securities says markets will continue to push Greece and the EU to the brink, until they come up with a credible plan to meet the country's financing needs. Traders shrug off an under-subscribed 30-year bund auction Wednesday, noting the bond wasn't particularly cheap and there is still plenty of supply lined up in that part of the curve from other countries. Elsewhere, Germany received only EUR2.752 billion in bids vs EUR3 billion offered at the auction of its 4.75% July 2040 bund. On Thursday, Spain offers EUR3 billion in bonds. Euro zone data for tomorrow include flash PMI, flash consumer confidence indicator and balance of payments. The 2/10 bund yield curve steepens to 219.9bps vs 219.3bps Tuesday. June bunds are up 22bps at 123.73 and =benchmark 10-year is up at 101.42 to yield 3.077%, within a 3.059%-3.114% range. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1327 GMT [Dow Jones] Fed-funds futures traders continue to raise their bets for funds rate hike in 2H of this yr. Nov prices in 62% chance for FOMC to lift funds rate to 0.5% at Nov 2-3 meeting. That's up from 56% chance Tues, but contract still has catching up to do from fully priced status on Apr. 5. That's when monthly data showed job growth, and bolstered view that Fed tightening was necessary to curb inflation. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1335 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR has crawled back to the $1.3400 level, recovering from its lows but still below the late Tues level of $1.3445. There doesn't appear to have any particular headlines driving the recovery, with the move appearing more as a rebound from earlier selling on worries about Greece, said one New York \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist. "We're still waiting and watching the headlines as they relate to Greece,' he said. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1326 GMT [Dow Jones] Premier Aircraft Leasing is in the market with $188M in secured fixed rate notes, according to a term sheet. Joint leads are GS/JPM/Credit Agricole. The transaction is structured as a bond issuance to refinance a portion of the purchase price of two aircraft. Pricing is expected later this week. (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com) [ 04-21-10 1036ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100421e64l000ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
