ning was necessary to curb inflation. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1335 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR has crawled back to the $1.3400 level, recovering from its lows but still below the late Tues level of $1.3445. There doesn't appear to have any particular headlines driving the recovery, with the move appearing more as a rebound from earlier selling on worries about Greece, said one New York \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist. "We're still waiting and watching the headlines as they relate to Greece,' he said. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1326 GMT [Dow Jones] Premier Aircraft Leasing is in the market with $188M in secured fixed rate notes, according to a term sheet. Joint leads are GS/JPM/Credit Agricole. The transaction is structured as a bond issuance to refinance a portion of the purchase price of two aircraft. Pricing is expected later this week. (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1322 GMT [Dow Jones] US rate futures' flattening trend remains intact after \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  Tues omitted pledge to keep its key rate at ultra low 0.25% through 2Q. Short-term Eurodollar futures prices recently down as much as 3 BP, equating to slightly higher yields. Long-term Tsy futures prices up, amounting to lower rates. Jun 30-yr Tsy bonds climb to nearly 1-month price top of 117-09. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com) [ 04-21-10 1027ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100421e64l000ab\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
