\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4-Romanian leu jumps after surprise rate cut\b0\par\par\uc2 925 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2010\par 17:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Romania's c.bank makes surprise cut, leu shakes off\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trims early gains after euro slips\par \par \uc2  * Serb dealers report c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2     (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  budget)\par \par \uc2  By Dagmara Leszkowicz and Jason Hovet\par \par \uc2  WARSAW/PRAGUE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - The Romanian leu jumped to a three-month high on Tuesday, with dealers citing sales of euro reserves by local banks optimistic over their loan portfolios that offset a surprise half-percentage point interest rate cut.\par \par \uc2  Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly cut its benchmark rate to 7.5 percent, with the move raising concern over the return of weakening pressure. However, the leu shook it off and rose on some banks' need for local capital. [ID:nnLDE6041E9]\par \par \uc2  Several dealers said local banks were moving to reduce some of the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  provisions set aside last year, buoyed by a generally more stable leu, and the fading of a funding and political crisis in the European Union newcomer.\par \par \uc2  "Some banks are selling massive sums of euros to get money, from (last year's) provisioning for bad loans, for planned capital hikes because of losses incurred last year," said a Bucharest dealer.\par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were also stop losses recorded after the unit firmed beyond a 4.19 per euro level. The leu <EURRON=> bid up 0.9 percent at 4.178 to the euro by 1624 GMT.\par \par \uc2  Most analysts had expected the Romanian bank to hold fire on rates until February, when expected parliamentary approval of a 2010 budget bill would help secure the next tranche in its IMF-led aid package. [ID:nLDE6040Y2] [ID:nLDE5BR09P]\par \par \uc2  "We believe this decision could prove counter-productive and, even though we acknowledge that economic crisis in Romania is still very deep, there is not room for monetary easing in the present political and financial environment," said Lars Christensen of \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  in Copenhagen.\par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Serb \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 17 million euros in the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday to stem dinar <EURRSD=> declines after banks reported deals nearing all-time lows at 97.30/euro, dealers said. [ID:nLDE6041GD]\par \par \uc2  Other emerging Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a touch down, buoyed by better manufacturing sentiment to start the year after giving up early gains when the dollar recover against the euro, the region's reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nLDE6030EP]\par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty <EURPLN=> was 0.2 percent down against the euro. Hungary's forint <EURHUF=> fell some 0.2 percent against the euro while the Czech crown <EURCZK=> was off 0.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  BUDGETS AHEAD\par \par \uc2  Analysts said news from Monday that the Czech 2009 state budget deficit was almost five times higher than plan weighed on the crown, which has lost over 2 percent in the past month.\par \par \uc2 Ceska Sporitelna\uc2  recommended on Monday that investors go long crown as temporary adverse factors fade and a trade surplus adds supports along with lower dividend outflows.[ID:nLDE60407H]\par \par \uc2  Budget deficits, though, remain a risk in the region as it grapples with economic decline and many face election years.\par \par \uc2  In Hungary, where an IMF-led emergency aid has imposed tough fiscal conditions, a December surplus helped cut the full-year deficit to below the target. Meeting the target was a condition with the IMF package. [ID:nBUD005212] [ID:LDE6041JO]\par \par \uc2  Poland also expects its 2009 budget deficit to come in below a revised target of 27 billion zlotys but this could double in 2010. The overall budget gap could hit 7 percent of GDP.\par \par \uc2  Poland's finance ministry on Monday gave details of the debt supply for the first quarter. The news knocked bonds, which reversed their losses on Tuesday. [ID:nLDE6031EM]\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2009 \par Czech crown      <EURCZK=>   26.26    26.231  -0.11%   +0.22%\par Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>    4.09     4.082  -0.2%    +0.34%\par Hungarian forint <EURHUF=>  268.91   268.35   -0.21%   +0.54%\par Croatian kuna    <EURHRK=>    7.288    7.291  +0.04%   +0.29%\par Romanian leu     <EURRON=>    4.178    4.214  +0.86%   +1.42%\par Serbian dinar    <EURRSD=>   96.88    96.43   -0.46%   -1.03%\par Yield Spreads\par Czech treasury bonds <0#CZBMK=>\par 3-yr T-bond   CZ3YT=RR    -32 basis points to  70bps over bmk*\par 7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +82bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   CZ10YT=RR   +6 basis points to  +69bps over bmk*\par Hungarian treasury bonds <0#HUBMK=>\par 3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR    -2 basis points to  +568bps over bmk*\par 5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR    -3 basis points to  +507bps over bmk*\par 10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR  -1 basis points to  +445bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent.\par All data taken from Reuters at 1725 CET.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highli