\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , equities retreat despite Polish output\b0\par\par\uc2 848 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2009\par 17:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  fall with emerging markets as euro, stocks down\par \par \uc2 * Romania plans EUR 500 mln domestic T-bill sale\par \par \uc2 * Hungarian long-dated bond yields rise on auction\par \par \uc2 (Updates with new comments, Romanian auction result, plan)\par \par \uc2 By Jason Hovet and Sandor Peto\par \par \uc2 PRAGUE/BUDAPEST, Nov 19 (Reuters) - Central European assets retreated on Thursday as capital control concerns in other emerging markets triggered a pull-out of investors despite Polish figures confirming steady economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Brazil unveiled a new tax on Wednesday to curb capital inflows [ID:nLN18128104], and Russia could also consider measures, although it has no immediate plans.[ID:nLJ54381]\par \par \uc2 While analysts said capital controls in emerging European Union (EU) members were unlikely, the gloomier global sentiment pushed \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , equities and bonds lower in the region, reducing the past weeks' gains.\par \par \uc2 "The region has been benefiting from a weakening dollar and strengthening equities, but that looks over now," a Prague-based dealer said. "It is still risk on/risk off."\par \par \uc2 The crown <EURCZK=>, the zloty <EURPLN=> and the forint <EURHUF=> have gained about three percent versus the euro since the last bout of risk aversion early this month.\par \par \uc2 A Czech rate setter repeated a call on Thursday for looser monetary conditions to stem crown strength, after a proposal for a rate cut was outvoted earlier this month.[ID:nPRG003790]\par \par \uc2 The three \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed 0.7 percent by 1510 GMT, although \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a 1.2 percent annual fall in Poland's industrial output -- less\par than analysts' 2.0 percent forecast -- underpinned expectations\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for steady recovery.[ID:nLJ409038]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Poland has been the only EU member which has escaped recession. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Hungary where the economy is seen contracting by about 6.5 percent this year<HUGDP1> is expected to cut its base rate further on Monday.[ID:nLI234800]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The forint can ease further towards 270," one Budapest-based dealer said. "But even that would not prevent a 50 basis point rate cut, unless there is a bigger weakening and an even bigger slump in equity markets."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA PLANS DOMESTIC EURO PAPER\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungary's fiscal plans were approved by the International Monetary Fund early this week, while the IMF has halted talks with neighbouring Romania which has also resorted to international aid like Hungary.[ID:nL18462411]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The delay in the talks makes it more difficult for the government to finance itself.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Thursday Romania sold just 264 million lei worth of three-year bonds at its 10 percent ceiling, and later the finance ministry announced that it planned to sell 500 million euros in one-year Treasury bills in the domestic market on Nov. 26.[ID:nBUC003556]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The leu bucked the regional trend, trading flat against the euro to hold a five-week high before the first round of presidential elections on Sunday and with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk hanging over the unit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Average yields set at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's government bond auctions were lower than two weeks ago, but rose from Wednesday's secondary market levels. Mainly five-year bonds were hit, with yields rising 20 basis points, after low demand at the auctions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Interest focused on shorter bonds which indicates longer term uncertainty," one trader said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2009 \par  Czech crown      <EURCZK=>  25.605   25.42    -0.72%   +4.48%\par  Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>   4.132    4.101   -0.75%   -0.41%\par  Hungarian forint <EURHUF=> 267.4    265.46    -0.73%   -1.44%\par  Croatian kuna    <EURHRK=>   7.321    7.315   -0.08%   +0.6%\par  Romanian leu     <EURRON=>   4.273    4.272   -0.02%   -6.05%\par  Serbian dinar    <EURRSD=>  94.29    94.27    -0.02%   -5.1%\par  Yield Spreads\par  Czech treasury bonds <0#CZBMK=>\par  3-yr T-bond   CZ3YT=RR  -12 basis points to  104bps over bmk*\par  7-yr T-bond   CZ7YT=RR    0 basis points to  +112bps over bmk*\par  10-yr T-bond  CZ10YT=RR  -4 basis points to  +93bps over bmk*\par  Hungarian treasury bonds <0#HUBMK=>\par  3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR   +2 basis points to  +531bps over bmk*\par  5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR   +3 basis points to  +479bps over bmk*\par  10-yr T-bond  HU10YT=RR  +2 basis points to  +412bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent. All data taken from Reuters at 1610 CET. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  percent change calculated from the daily domestic close at 1600 GMT. For related news and prices, click on the codes in brackets: All emerging market news [EMRG] Spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 