\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 3-CEE assets extend loss, may ease further\b0\par\par\uc2 868 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2009\par 16:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stocks fall sharply\par \par \uc2 * Poland holds rates steady at 3.5 percent\par \par \uc2 (Recast with new prices, comments)\par \par \uc2 By Marius Zaharia and Sandor Peto\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST/BUDAPEST, Oct 28 (Reuters) - Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to multi-month lows on Wednesday and bond yields rose as investors focused on the region's fiscal and political risks amid new doubts over the global economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its main interest rate on hold as expected, but other central banks in the region, concerned by recession, are expected to cut their interest rates further.\par \par \uc2 As the region's assets remain exposed to global sentiment changes, government bond yields rose and stocks fell like in other emerging markets.[ID:nLS54627]\par \par \uc2 "Profit-taking, risk aversion, sentiment change, correction? Call it as you like, the vulnerability of the CEE \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is obviously unchanged, not to mention rates...," one Budapest-based trader said.\par \par \uc2 The retreat may be more lasting and go deeper this time than similar falls in the past months, some market watchers said.\par \par \uc2 "We today -- or within the last couple of days -- have broken the 100 days moving averages on the zloty, the forint, the crown, the lei, the lira and the rand," said Lars Christensen, analysts at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He said Danske's scorecards for the units, which track risk indicators, turned even gloomier on Wednesday, including the zloty which is often used as a proxy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the region even though Poland has escaped recession unlike other states.\par \par \uc2 The zloty <EURPLN=> shed 1.1 percent against the euro to 4.261, after the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept rates on hold at an all-time low at 3.5 percent.[ID:nLS648224]\par \par \uc2 RATES, POLITICS WEIGH\par \par \uc2 The forint <EURHUF=> led losses, hitting a six-week low per euro at 274.50, before regaining some ground. It was bid at 273.26 at 1447 GMT, still weaker by 1.45 percent from Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Hungarian bond yields continued to rise. But long-dated yields corrected slightly downwards from morning levels, and the spread between 10-year yields at 7.43 percent and 3-year yields at 7.30 narrowed from 34 basis points a day ago.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at 7.0 percent is well above the Polish and Czech levels, but the bank is expected to cut rates further as the country struggles with rising unemployment, while its high external debt keeps it vulnerable to market shocks.\par \par \uc2 General Electric\uc2  said on Wednesday that it would cut nearly 2,700 jobs in Hungary in the next two years.[ID:nLS21901]\par \par \uc2 The yield curve, which was below 7 percent days ago, may reach 8 percent soon, though the prospect of rate cuts can push it downwards again if the global mood improves, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The leu <EURRON=>, pressured by uncertainty following the collapse of Romania's government earlier this month, traded at seven-month lows, but the daily move was less spectacular.\par \par \uc2 It fell 0.3 percent from the previous close, with investors fearing a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  close to 4.3 per euro.\par \par \uc2 Romania, like \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 , relies on funding from the International Monetary Fund and markets fear Romania's political turmoil will hurt its chances of keeping IMF cash flowing.\par \par \uc2 An IMF mission started its second review of Romania's 20 billion euro bailout as parliament holds hearings for ministers proposed by Prime Minister designate Lucian Croitoru, who is widely expected to fail to get political backing.[ID:nLS606619]\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, neighbouring Moldova agreed to a $590 million \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stand-by loan from the IMF.[ID:nLS675123]   \par  --------------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT--------------------\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                    close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                             change   change\par                                             today    in 2009 \par  Czech crown      <EURCZK=>  26.428   26.201   -0.86%    +1.23%\par  Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>   4.261    4.216   -1.06%    -3.43%\par  Hungarian forint <EURHUF=> 273.26   269.29    -1.45%    -3.55%\par  Croatian kuna    <EURHRK=>   7.222    7.218   -0.06%    +1.98%\par  Romanian leu     <EURRON=>   4.302    4.29    -0.28%    -6.69%\par  Serbian dinar    <EURRSD=>  93.18    93.113   -0.07%    -3.97%\par  \par  Hungarian treasury bonds <0#HUBMK=>\par  3-yr T-bond   HU3YT=RR   +30 basis points to  +553bps over bmk*\par  5-yr T-bond   HU5YT=RR   +25 basis points to  +491bps over bmk*\par  10-yr T-bond   HU10YT=RR +9 basis points to  +416bps over bmk*\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Benchmark is German bond equivalent. All data taken from Reuters at 1547 CET. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  percent change calculated from the daily domestic close at 1600 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For related news and prices, click on the codes in brackets: All emerging market news [EMRG] \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates Eastern