\par\par \b \uc2 Forint around 310/euro was stability risk -cbanker\b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2009\par 20:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, April 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally and launched other measures to support the forint in March as lasting levels around 310 to the euro could have threatened financial stability, a deputy governor said.\par \par \uc2 The forint <EURHUF=D2> hit record lows past 317 to the euro early in March in a broader sell-off in central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Hungarian central bankers hardly ever comment on specific exchange rate levels.\par \par \uc2 In Hungary, similarly to Poland and Romania, many households and corporate borrowers took out loans in euros and Swiss francs in the past several years and a lasting significant \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening increases their repayments.\par \par \uc2 "In our case depreciation had reached a level where we believe that in the longer term it could have caused serious risks to financial stability, this was at about 310 (versus the euro)," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Ferenc Karvalits told a conference on Wednesday at Budapest's Corvinus University.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also announced in March it would begin to convert European Union development funds for Hungary in the open market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The forint has since recovered and on Wednesday finished trade around two-month highs past 290 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Hungary became the first European Union member to seek financial aid last year, securing a $25.1 billion International Monetary Fund-led rescue loan to stave off financial collapse.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left interest rates on hold at 9.5 percent at its policy meeting in April in a unanimous decision, citing sustained uncertainty in domestic and global markets. "On the whole, I think that as the depreciation pressure was essentially a regional phenomenon, the solution of the problem will also be related to the assessment of the fundamentals of the region as a whole," Karvalits said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Krisztina Than and Gergely Szakacs)\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY-FORINT/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|HX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090429e54t001ls\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
