\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar, euro soar vs Swiss franc as SNB  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 02:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar, euro jump vs Swiss franc after SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * SNB to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avert deflation risk\par \par \uc2 * SNB move to benefit other European emerging markets (Updates prices, adds comment, changes byline)\par \par \uc2 By Nick Olivari\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, March 12 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar and euro jumped against the Swiss franc on Thursday after the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  said it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as it faced the growing risk of deflation.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was implementing its decision to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The SNB also cut interest rates on Thursday by a quarter percentage point to a historic low, offering three-, six- and 12-month funds at 0.05 percent.\par \par \uc2 The SNB, which last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August 1995, further said it will buy not only foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but bonds as well. Switzerland is facing its worst recession in over three decades. For the SNB statement, click on [ID:nSNBTEXT]. Past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  [ID:nLC337364].\par \par \uc2 A "very, very strong statement from the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  about what they are doing and about to do," said Karthik Sankaran, Portfolio Manager and Principal at Covepoint Capital Advisors LLC In New York. "They are the first \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is actually using the purchase of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a means of quantitative easing."\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon New York trading, the dollar rose 2.96 percent to 1.1876 francs <CHF=>, on track for its biggest one-day gain since August 1995, at current prices. It rose as high as 1.1965 francs, a three-month high, according to Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc is one of the world's most traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at times prized as a safe haven for investors.\par \par \uc2 The euro climbed to 1.5302 Swiss francs, the highest since December. It last traded at 1.5234 <EURCHF=>, up 2.9 percent, the euro's best day ever against the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SNB's move to zero rates and quantitative easing was expected, traders said, but the immediate move to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a surprise.\par \par \uc2 Bank of New York-Mellon senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Michael Woolfolk said "the way this was communicated was intended at maximizing its shock value." He said there were no hints from SNB officials ahead of time that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be immediate.\par \par \uc2 "They changed their economic outlook, they not only lowered interest rates to effectively zero but also announced quantitative easing and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This was the full monty," Woolfolk said.\par \par \uc2 POLAND, \b \highlight22\uc2 HUNGARY\b0 \highlight\uc2  BENEFIT FROM SNB ACTION\par \par \uc2 Quantitative easing has been deployed by central banks in countries including Britain, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is buying assets with newly created money.\par \par \uc2 Marc Chandler, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York, said the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should ease pressure on Poland and \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 , two European emerging market countries seriously hit by the global credit crisis.\par \par \uc2 These two countries had taken advantage of ultra-low Swiss interest rates, borrowing heavily in Swiss francs and investing in riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 "The strength of the Swiss franc compounded their woes. Today's dramatic weakening of the Swiss franc may ease this pressure," said Chandler.\par \par \uc2 Gains in the dollar versus the Swiss franc boosted the greenback against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the euro and sterling.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell 0.1 percent to $1.2871 <EUR=>. The euro zone single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also pressured by comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet that euro zone interest rates could be cut further. [ID:nLC956324]\par \par \uc2 The ECB cut its benchmark rate to a record low 1.5 percent last week and economists expect it to cut to 1.0 percent, most likely in April.\par \par \uc2 Sterling rose 0.1 percent to $1.3867 <GBP=>.\par \par \uc2 The SNB news overshadowed all other events and data in the market including U.S. retail sales numbers that were better than expected and weekly jobless claims data that were not far from analysts' forecasts. [ID:nN12352975]\par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar erased early losses, partly because of firmer U.S. stocks, still one of the key drivers in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Stocks were lifted by energy shares and the U.S. retail sales report. The dollar rose 0.6 percent to 97.81 <JPY=>. (Additional reporting by Steven C. Johnson and Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss; Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  