\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Mkts Await Key Hungary, Poland News\b0\par\par\uc2 By Edith Balazs   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 1,729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 04:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par Local/GMT \par 0900/0800 Hungarian February CPI \par 0900/0800 Czech final 4Q GDP \par 0930/0830 Poland \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President speaks at Polish Banking Forum \par 1000/0900 Poland Finance Minister speaks at Polish Banking Forum \par 1230/1130 Poland Finance Ministry offers two- and five-year T-Bonds at \par           monthly switch auction \par N/A       Russia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Severstal\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Mobile TeleSystems report 2008 earnings \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--Hungary's February inflation data and comments by Polish monetary and fiscal leaders will take center stage Wednesday as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seem to regain some of their footing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Slawomir Skrzypek and Finance Minister Jacek Rostowski are both scheduled to address the Polish Banking Association. The focus remains on the zloty, which has achieved a precarious stability of late, and on the feasibility of the government's fast-track timetable for adopting the euro.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's Polish switch auction may also help set the tone on regional bond markets, especially if the finance ministry is successful in placing significant amounts of its two- and five-year benchmarks. In recent weeks, investors have steered clear of tenors longer than two years, a reluctance that has prompted the ministry to ramp up offerings of 26-week and 52-week paper.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's inflation reading for February is likely to fall below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 3% target for the first time since mid-2006, analysts say. Inflation is forecast in a poll of 10 economists by Dow Jones Newswires to have slowed to 2.7% in February versus 3.1% in January. Nonetheless the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to react with lower interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "Fundamentally, the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to cut interest rates to stimulate economic activity, but the recent dramatic weakening of the forint limits any further aggressive monetary easing at the moment," \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 In Moscow, \uc2 Severstal\uc2 's and Mobile TeleSystems's (MBT) fourth-quarter results will enable investors to better calculate the costs of the financial crisis for the country's steel and mobile communications sectors. Analysts expect a net loss from the country's largest steel producer, \uc2 Severstal\uc2 , which will suffer from revaluation of its inventories, while the profit of Russia's top cellular provider by users is likely to fall, largely due to the sharp depreciation of the ruble.\par \par \uc2 The Czech statistics office is due to release its final fourth-quarter gross domestic growth reading. The final figure for annual growth is expected to be revised downward from the preliminary 1% growth rate, according to a recent Dow Jones Newswires poll of analysts. The data are likely to underscore signs of easing inflationary pressures as the export-focused economy is hit by slowing western-European demand for its exports, namely cars and electronic devices.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                    2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 26.900-60  26.896-46  +0.01  26.981  26.910   +0.55 \par EUR/HUF 303.60-00  303.85-15  -0.08  303.95  303.20  +15.20 \par EUR/PLN 4.631-35   4.6380-10  -0.15  4.6360  4.628   +12.54 \par USD/RUB 35.080-90  35.049-55  +0.09  35.101  34.976  +14.92 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint continued its rebound Tuesday, moving closer to the 300 level as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and efforts aimed at talking up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appear successful. However, market players might test the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's tolerance level of forint weakness again in the coming days, a dealer said. While The \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Hungary\f28 \uc2 \f2  is ready to implement further measures if it deems necessary to defend the Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the monetary policy tools are limited, \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Hungary\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor Andras Simor said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish zloty firmed Tuesday on the back of improving global sentiment. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was trading at 4.67 against the euro Tuesday afternoon and is expected to head toward 4.60 Wednesday, a dealer said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Czech koruna will be under pressure Wednesday after strengthening almost 2% to the euro and almost 3% to the dollar Tuesday, analysts said. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's gains followed a report by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  that the Czech Republic's macroeconomic outlook is not acutely at risk, unlike some other countries in the region. The euro/koruna moved below 27 for the first time since mid-January on the news.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With regard to the Russian ruble, Troika Dialog said "the market has not met strong support at RUB40.00 (against a dollar-euro basket)...We think that the basket will move lower next week." The Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reached a three-week high against the dollar-euro basket the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  uses for guiding its daily exchange rate. The ruble closed at RUB39.28 against the basket, up almost 2%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par HUNGARIAN BOND YIELDS - The three-year bond yield was at 13.90% late Tuesday from 14.25% late Monday; five-year was at 13.20% from 13.30%; 10-year was at 12.15% from 12.30%. \par  \par POLISH BOND YIELDS - The two-year average yield was at 5.75% late Tuesday from 5.83% late Monday; five-year unchanged at 6.10%; 10-year was at 6.33% from 6.38%. \par  \par CZECH BOND YIELD - 10-year benchmark was unchanged at 4.92%. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungarian treasuries firmed throughout Tuesday's session, boosted by a continuous strengthening of the forint. Market direction hinges on the forint, if the euro/forint cross dips below the 300 level, yields could come down by 50-80bp, a trader said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Polish treasury bonds firmed Tuesday follow a rising zloty on improving global sentiment, traders said. "Finally, we can see liquidity on the market," a local trader said. He added that healthy demand was likely at the Finance Ministry's switch auction Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG20                    1481.42   gain   25.75  up 1.8% \par BUX                      9870.31   loss  149.88  dn 1.5% \par PX                        660.2    gain    19.8  up 3.1% \par RTS                       634.92   gain    58.5  up 10.0% \par DJ Stoxx EU Enlarged 15:  1212,22  gain   45,47  up 3.9% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN WARSAW: Stocks rose Tuesday on improved global sentiment. With the benchmark index breaking strong resistance at 1450, it may test 1600, a local broker said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN PRAGUE: Local stocks rallied on the coattails of U.S. markets Tuesday, with financial stocks gaining strongly on the back of positive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  news flow. "The question is whether the markets are strong enough to maintain these gains," a local trader said, adding that while prices are still attractive, after sharp gains, profit taking early Wednesday can't be ruled out.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN BUDAPEST: Stocks failed to benefit from improving global sentiment Tuesday and all blue chips ended in the red with the exception of OTP. "The selling pressure on (domestic) stocks appears relentless," a trader said. There remains room for limited gains Wednesday if U.S. markets close higher, a trader said, but the BUX is likely to stabilize around the 10000 level for now.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN MOSCOW: "There's momentum on Russian markets from the expectations of a higher oil price," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2 's head of trading Maxim Gulevich, but he warns that stocks could surrender Tuesday's 10% gains if the Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries agrees on production cuts and speculative investors in Russian stocks fix their recent profits. The Russian Trading System finished at 634.92 Tuesday, close to its highest point of the session, returning to the level seen during the first trading week of the year. Investors will focus tomorrow on MTS and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Severstal\f28 \uc2 \f2 . [ 03-10-09 2357ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  OTHER NEWS \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HUNGARY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : The \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has carried out active \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot market to defend the Hungarian forint, remarks made Tuesday by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Andras Simor indicate. "We are active in the market, we buy forints in exchange for euros; how many forints we buy and at what rate we won't disclose," Simor said in an interview with private television channel TV2.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: EU finance ministers approved the European Commission's assessment of Hungary's convergence programme at a meeting in Brussels on Tuesday, Finance Ministry state secretary Almos Kovacs said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUSSIA: Russian ambassador to the European Union, Vladimir Chizov, dismissed Tuesday the Nabucco pipeline as not viable, rejected the Energy Charter Treaty as not credible and called for global oil price stability.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUSSIA: Russia will have a one-year federal budget for 2009 and will return to the policy of three-year budget planning for 2010-2012, Deputy Prime Minister and Finance Minister Alexei Kudrin said at a news briefing following a government session dealing with amendments to the Budget Code on Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUSSIA: The fundamental Russian-Hungarian agreement on the South Stream natural gas pipeline project signed on Tuesday, is "a serious forward step in concretizing our work" said Russian President Dmitry Medvedev, who praised the general state of relations between the two countries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Polish copper producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 KGHM Polska Miedz SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (KGH.WA) will freeze 2009 wages, the company said in a statement Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The Czech Republic's current account deficit widened in the fourth quarter, compared with the third quarter, as the trade balance swung into a deficit, the Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romanian Foreign Minister Lazar Comanescu stated here on Monday that his country is keen on developing and enhancing cooperation with the Gulf Cooperation Countries in the fields of politics, economy, commerce, and investment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: The European Union is ready to provide financial support to Romania to see it through the global economic slowdown, it said in a statement late Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: The cost of insuring Romania's sovereign debt against default fell Tuesday, as details of a potential loan package from the European Union and the International Monetary Fund emerged.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BULGARIA: Fast-track entry into the euro zone isn't Bulgaria's first priority, Bulgarian Finance Minister Plamen Oresharski said Tuesday. "It is not our first priority - our first priority is macroeconomic and fiscal stability," Oresharski said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Edith Balazs, Dow Jones Newswires; +361-267-0623; edith.balazs@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (David McQuaid in Warsaw, Sean Carney in Prague, William Bland in Moscow contributed to this report.) [ 03-10-09 2358ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020090311e53b0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
