\par\par \b \uc2 DJ 2nd UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bker Implies Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 18:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds further details from interview.)\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  has carried out active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot market to defend the Hungarian forint, remarks made Tuesday by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Andras Simor indicate.\par \par \uc2 "We are active in the market, we buy forints in exchange for euros; how many forints we buy and at what rate we won't disclose," Simor said in an interview with private television channel TV2.\par \par \uc2 Simor reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to defend the forint, which recently fell to all-time lows against the euro, by all its policy means. The forint has fallen to "sensitive levels," which is reflected by a verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council Sunday, Simor said.\par \par \uc2 However, the MPC hasn't committed to an interest rate decision in either direction for the next rate-setting meeting and the rate decision of the March 23 meeting is still undecided, Simor added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said Sunday that it would channel European Union funds to the forint market to support the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank and the government expect the amount available will total over EUR1.4 billion this year, Simor said Tuesday, adding that this should suffice "not for one week or one month but should serve as guidance for the whole year." He said the finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have no agreement yet as to how much of the total would be converted on the forint market.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian banking sector has accommodated the weaker forint levels, and has continued to operate safely, said Simor.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no exchange rate level that it considers to be detrimental to the economy, the bank governor said, adding that it continually adapts its view on the matter.\par \par \uc2 The fate of the forint in the longer term is in the hands of the government and hinges on regional sentiment, as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps can only have a temporary impact, Simor added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action provides the government with time to come up with fiscal measures, Simor said. He added that Hungary should reduce budget spending, lower taxes and raise employment levels under a long-term, coherent and comprehensive action plan spanning the next four to five years.\par \par \uc2 The country has more urgent and important tasks at the moment than setting a target date for entering the European Exchange Rate Mechanism 2, the anteroom to the euro, Simor added.\par \par \uc2 -By Edith Balazs and Margit Feher, Dow Jones Newswires; +361-267-0623; edith.balazs@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 10, 2009 13:48 ET (17:48 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090821e53a0mz1a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
