\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Forint Strength Seen Short-Lived\b0\par\par\uc2 By Edith Balazs   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 1,272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 05:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par Local/GMT 0900/0800 Czech power company \f28 \uc2 \f2 CEZ AS\f28 \uc2 \f2  head of sales Alan Svoboda speaks at conference \par 1100/1000 Poland insurer \f28 \uc2 \f2 PZU SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  4Q results \par 1130/1030 Hungary auctions 3-month T-Bills \par 1200/1100 Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  2-week bill \par N/A       Poland February unemployment estimate \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets remain in the spotlight following the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's straightforward verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Sunday night aimed at putting a floor under the plummeting forint.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Comments from the Monetary Policy Council indicating that the bank was ready to deploy its full arsenal in the defense of the forint, including the conversion of European Union funds on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, helped stop the slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but analysts and market participants expect the impact to be short-lived.\par \par \uc2 "The announcement could stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at least in the short run, but we cannot say for sure, that other measures, such as an interest rate hike, might not be needed," CIB Bank said.\par \par \uc2 "The tools at the disposal of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are limited to improve confidence toward Hungary: the fiscal side should also do its job," CIB added.\par \par \uc2 It's unlikely that the forint will dip below the 300 level against the euro unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveils further details of its planned \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or actually hikes interest rates, a trader said.\par \par \uc2 In Poland, markets should get a first look at the February labor market when the labor ministry issues preliminary unemployment figures. The headline jobless rate is seen rising to 10.8%, from 10.5% in January and 9.5% in December.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                    2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 27.500-40  27.505-45  -0.02  27.505  27.530   +2.79 \par EUR/HUF 309.56-85  310.35-65  -0.25  310.10  309.85  +17.46 \par EUR/PLN 4.7450-00  4.7423-63  +0.06  4.7450  4.7500  +15.31 \par USD/RUB 35.558-79  35.623-56  -0.18  35.886  35.555  +16.49 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint recovered Monday as a result of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's straightforward verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the weekend. The forint hit an all-time record of 317.59 against the euro last week and has lost 22% against the euro since the start of 2009. "The forint should be stabilized around 300 for the short term but mere verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't be enough to push the cross that low," a local dealer said. \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  also warned against overplaying the positives from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's statement of channeling E.U. funds through the forint market noting that such a move was probably already discounted in the market after Poland's similar measures a week ago.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish zloty got only faint and fleeting support from Hungary's weekend effort to talk up the forint and hints from Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Slawomir Skrzypek that direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the markets is no longer beyond the pale. "It looks like investors are dropping last week's differentiated approach to countries in the region," said BPH Bank Chief Economist Maja Goettig in a research note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Czech koruna is likely to remain in a wide trading band to the euro Tuesday as expectations for a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate increase this month are offset by weak data from Monday showing lower-than expected inflation in February and weak exports. Oldrich Myslivec, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at Patria Finance, said the support level for euro/Czech koruna this week seems to be 27.90, while the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pairs find resistance at 27.20.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par HUNGARIAN BOND YIELDS - The three-year bond yield was at 14.25% late Monday from 14.10% late Friday; five-year was at 13.30% from 13.20%; 10-year was at 12.30% from 12.25%. \par  \par POLISH BOND YIELDS - The two-year average yield was at 5.83% late Monday from 5.72% late Friday; five-year was at 6.10% from 6.09%; 10-year was 6.38% from 6.39%. \par  \par CZECH BOND YIELD - 10-year benchmark was 4.92% late Monday, unchanged from late Friday. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungarian treasuries failed to profit from the forint's weakening Monday and yields rose across the curve amid extremely slight volumes. There are hardly any deals, everyone is waiting for more news from the fiscal and/or monetary policy front," a trader said. Bonds are likely to tread water amid continued light volumes as foreign investors will continue to shun local debt until more news on the intended \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or a potential rate hike, he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Polish treasury bonds drifted lower Monday with the short end bearing the brunt on news the finance ministry will offer two-year paper at Wednesday's switch auction. Volumes were low and expected to stay that way until Wednesday's tender, with zloty moves likely to continue setting the direction on the five- and 10-year segment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG20                    1455.67   loss   20.79  dn 1.4% \par BUX                     10020.19   gain  139.82  up 1.4% \par PX                        640.4    loss    3.0   dn 0.5% \par DJ Stoxx EU Enlarged 15: 1166.75   loss  1.21    dn 0.1% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN WARSAW: Stocks gave back last week's gains Monday mostly due to bad news from U.K. banking sector. Low volumes suggest the market remains relatively resilient and 1,450 should support WIG20 for now, a local fund manager said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN PRAGUE: Financial stocks gained Monday thanks to low prices, strong gains in Hungary's OTP and investors setting up new long positions, a trader said. The trader added that Telefonica O2, closing -3.4% at CZK387, is likely to rebound Tuesday as investors buy when the stock dips below CZK390.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN BUDAPEST: Stocks closed up Monday on \f28 \uc2 \f2 OTP Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's continued gains. OTP ended up 7.2% after surging 12.2% in heavy trade. The stock could maintain its momentum for the next couple of sessions, thus lending support to the benchmark BUX index as well, a trader said. [ 03-10-09 0002ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  OTHER NEWS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Slawomir Skrzypek said Monday he is "not happy" with the level of Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the zloty and that it doesn't reflect economic fundamentals.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech annual inflation of 2% in February was half a percentage point above the Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's forecast, driven higher by annual rises in prices for food and fuels that were in turn influenced by the weak koruna, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SLOVAKIA: Slovak industrial output tumbled 27% in January against a year ago, posting its biggest fall in 10 years due to the global economic downturn, the Slovak Statistics Office said Monday.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HUNGARY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : The Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's plan to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets -- using funds it gets from the European Union to do so -- helped boost the forint on Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: An International Monetary Fund mission will visit Romania later this month to hold discussions on a potential IMF loan program for Romania, the IMF said Monday in a statement, news agency Mediafax reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania needs a foreign loan as a "safety belt" for the private sector and the current account deficit, not to finance its public debt and budget deficit, Romanian President Traian Basescu said Monday speaking in parliament, news agency Mediafax reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Edith Balazs, Dow Jones Newswires; +361-267-0623; edith.balazs@dowjones.com [ 03-10-09 0002ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020090310e53a0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\s