\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bker: Verbal  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Enough-MTI\b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2009\par 11:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds further comments, background.)\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--The effectiveness of the concerted verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday by the Polish, Hungarian, Czech and Romanian central banks will only show in the long term, Hungarian state-run news agency MTI quoted the deputy governor of the \uc2 National Bank of Hungary\uc2 , Ferenc Karvalits, as saying late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "It's not possible to manage the exchange rate solely with verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," MTI quoted Karvalits as saying.\par \par \uc2 In an unprecedented, coordinated move, Central and Eastern European central banks said Monday that the recent dive of the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was excessive and unfounded by economic fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to follow up with the appropriate interest rate steps," Karvalits said.\par \par \uc2 He added that the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council decided Monday not to continue its series of rate cuts. The doubts that investors feel about Central and Eastern Europe, which "could lead to a risk shock, had made the bank proceed more slowly," Karvalits said.\par \par \uc2 "We expect that, with a stabilization of the exchange rate, a calm-down of the negative perceptions we can rethink how to proceed from here," Karvalits said.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian forint is about 15% weaker against the euro than at the end of last year, and 25% weaker than in June 2008.\par \par \uc2 Both forint volatility and the extent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakening have posed a significant challenge for the economy, Karvalits said. He added that there are ways of tackling such risks, but at a cost.\par \par \uc2 It would be preferable for the forint to stabilize in the longer term, Karvalits said.\par \par \uc2 But he added that a floating exchange rate provides an appropriate framework for a small and open economy, such as Hungary's, to accommodate external economic shocks.\par \par \uc2 A year ago, Hungary scrapped its trading band-based exchange rate mechanism - which allowed the forint to trade up or down by 15% around a midpoint set against the euro - and opted instead to float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  freely.\par \par \uc2 The forint's recent devaluation was an overreaction of the market, Karvalits said. The forint will correct in the long term so long as Hungary's economy becomes healthier, Karvalits said, although he added that this doesn't necessarily means the forint will recover to previous levels.\par \par \uc2 Agency Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mti.hu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.mti.hu}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Margit Feher, Dow Jones Newswires; +361-267-0622; margit.feher@dowjones.com [ 26-02-09 1028GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090226e52q000oe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
