\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE:Hungary Ctrl Bk: Major Devaluation Must Be Avoided\b0\par\par\uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2009\par 18:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds further details on forint, analysts' comments)\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--The Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to act to prevent excessive forint weakness and volatility, the \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday as part of a coordinated verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the central banks of Central and Eastern Europe.\par \par \uc2 "While some exchange rate adjustment is indeed appropriate in these economies, excessive depreciation, which is not justified by economic fundamentals, can be disruptive and should be avoided," the bank said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "The Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to take action if necessary to prevent disruptive movements in the forint's exchange rate," the bank added.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the forint hit an all-time low against the euro as emerging Europe, including Hungary, was hit by another wave of poor investor confidence in the region.\par \par \uc2 The concerted action of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was positive, analysts said. Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened in response.\par \par \uc2 "This is positive for the markets in the region, at least in the short term," said \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  chief analyst Lars Christensen.\par \par \uc2 "That said, we doubt that verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is enough - the CEE central banks might need to hike rates, or get outside help, for example from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We would therefore be looking for possible comments from the ECB on this issue," Christensen added.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian Monetary Policy Council discussed Monday only the option of holding interest rates steady, Governor Andras Simor said.\par \par \uc2 "The current market conditions played a decisive part in the decision," Simor said.\par \par \uc2 Future interest rate cuts will hinge on financial market stability and capital flows, while the rate of the Hungarian forint will remain a significant factor for rate decisions, Simor added.\par \par \uc2 "The forint rate plays a significant role in monetary policy decisions because of its impact on inflation and financial stability," Simor said at a press conference after the Monetary Policy Council decided to keep the key interest rate unchanged at 9.50%.\par \par \uc2 Hungary, which has cut interest rates four times over the past three months, will likely slow the pace of easing from now on, said economist Piotr Kalisz at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Monday's decision to keep the key rate unchanged reflects the bank's determination to maintain interest rates at relatively high levels as long as the forint remains under strong depreciation pressure, said Kalisz, who expects the key rate to be cut in 25-basis-point steps over the rest of the year, to be at 8.50% by year-end.\par \par \uc2 Simor declined to comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the open market in defense of the forint, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't comment in future about any possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  either, the governor added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now projects that annual average inflation will be 3.7% this year and 2.8% next year, with the forecasts based on a forint rate very close to the current market level, in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecast-generation rules, Simor said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasts that Hungary's economy will contract 3.5% this year and shrink by 0.5% next year.\par \par \uc2 In its last Inflation Report in November, the bank saw this year's inflation rate between 3.1%-3.4% and next year's inflation rate between 1.5%-1.9%. It had projected this year's economic contraction at a maximum 1.7% and forecast economic growth of between 0.5%-2% for next year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Web site: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mnb.hu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.mnb.hu}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Margit Feher, Dow Jones Newswires; +36-20-925-2364; margit.feher@dowjones.com [ 23-02-09 1727GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090223e52n000oc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
