\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 5-C.bankers move to lift  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  as  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  holds rates\b0\par\par\uc2 1,009 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2009\par 17:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Central bankers verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firm on c.bank talk, better global sentiment\par \par \uc2 * Hungary leaves interest rates unchanged\par \par \uc2 * Poland sticks to euro plans\par \par \uc2 (Adds fixed income, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Marius Zaharia and Jason Hovet\par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST/PRAGUE, Feb 23 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty, Czech crown and Hungarian forint jumped on Monday, wiping out recent losses after central bankers in the region said in a coordinated verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that falls were overdone.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left rates unchanged at 9.5 percent, marking a likely pause or reversal in many of emerging Europe's monetary policy easing cycles as looser rates have added to swiftly depreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  already hurt by a sinking economic outlook. [ID:nLN588670]\par \par \uc2 Central Europe's central banks took the unprecedented step of joint verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday to support their region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that sank to multi-year or record lows in the past week, saying their sharp drop did not reflect their economic fundamentals. [ID:nLN571478] [ID:nLN466658]\par \par \uc2 "We do need to see these words backed by hard action, but this is a concerted defence by the central banks of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Martin Blum, emerging strategist with \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  in Vienna.\par \par \uc2 "...It's a good sign that the countries are speaking together, they have been a little bit too relaxed previously."\par \par \uc2 The Czech, Hungarian and Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped around 1 percent to add to strong gains from the morning after the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but later gave up those gains.\par \par \uc2 By 1603 GMT, the forint <EURHUF=> had risen 2.35 percent since Friday to the strong side of 300 per euro, and the Polish zloty <EURPLN=> gained 2.3 percent. The Czech crown <EURCZK=> added 1.8 percent, while Romania's leu <EURRON=> traded even.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also helped by a media report that said the U.S. government could raise its stake in \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , which lifted stocks and weakened the dollar. [ID:nSP428865]\par \par \uc2 Hungarian bond yields dropped sharply from recent highs on the firmer \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and strengthening swap rates, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Markets had clawed back some losses last week to cap a rollercoaster five days as worries over emerging Europe's foreign debt exposure grew, and today's gains have put \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  up on par with closing levels on Feb. 13.\par \par \uc2 The steep falls last week had rattled western banking stocks, prompted policymakers to verbally step in, and many strategists called the rapid declines overdone. [ID:nLJ819234]\par \par \uc2 Poland had converted EU funds to prop up the zloty last week, while Hungary's prime minister asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to explore "unconventional" means to stem forint losses.\par \par \uc2 "I think the forint will target 300 again in the short term," a Budapest dealer said. "But the situation changes very quickly... Guessing what comes next is something like playing the lottery now."\par \par \uc2 The weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have caused borrowing costs to rise for households and businesses in Hungary, Romania and Poland that sought cheaper foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans in the past -- but give small relief to exporters that have seen demand for their goods sink in the recession-hit euro zone.\par \par \uc2 Volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rising budget deficits in the wake of the global economic crisis have also put doubt on government's ambitions to adopt the euro zone's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Poland -- which aims to join the euro zone the soonest after central Europe's smallest state Slovakia switched to euros this year -- a deputy finance minister said the country could enter the testing ground ERM-2 by early June. [ID:nLN516368]\par \par \uc2 Polish companies have been hurt badly by wrong-way bets the zloty would continue to rise from record highs last summer. [ID:nLL467650] The unit has been among the worst-performing emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since, and has lost 11.3 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 The forint is down 11.3 percent also in 2009, while the crown is off 5.3 percent and the leu 6.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Donald Tusk said on Friday the worst is past for the zloty [ID:nLK621374], but many analysts see more weakening before a second-half rebound for the region.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ----------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT-------------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                           