\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Hungary Seen Holding Rates Same\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 2,034 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2009\par 05:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TODAY'S CALENDAR \par  \par Local/GMT \par  \par 1200/1100 Poland 52-week T-bill auction, PLN1.3B-PLN1.8B on offer \par 1300/1200 Czech Energy conference with minister of energy, executives from local unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 RWE AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par 1400/1300 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  interest rate decision \par 1430/1330 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  presser \par 2400/2300 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Magyar Telekom\f28 \uc2 \f2  4Q earnings \par N/A Russian Public Holdiday in Russia, Armed Forces Day \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PRAGUE (Dow Jones)--Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steals the spotlight Monday with its much anticipated monetary policy decision that may foreshadow policy moves of other regional central banks as they all try to defend their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid worsening economic conditions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Hungarian central bankers find themselves between a rock and a hard place. The bank is expected to leave its key rate unchanged at 9.50% Monday, 11 out of the 16 bank economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires said. Of the remaining five, one expected a 100 basis-point rate cut, two a 50 basis-point cut and the other two a 25 basis-point rate cut.\par \par \uc2 With the forint hitting new lows against the euro recently and government bond yields climbing to new highs while the treasury market is in shambles, a rate cut could add fuel to the fire while a rate hike could prove ineffective, the polled economists said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's easing bias, however, is seen remaining intact as the economy is heading for a deep recession.\par \par \uc2 Polish market will be focused on the zloty and chances to sustain gains from the end of lastweek or at least to stabilize around recent levels of 4.72-4.75 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 The key factor which could define the fate of the zloty, analysts said, will be the status of the government's drive to join the European Union's Exchange Rate Mechanism, or ERM 2.\par \par \uc2 The euro push provided much needed support to the zloty when it was under heavy selling pressure from foreign investors last week.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                    2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par EUR/CZK 28.800-40  28.815-75  -0.05  28.825  28.840   +7.65 \par EUR/HUF 302.75-30  303.85-15  -0.36  302.80  302.30  +14.87 \par EUR/PLN 4.7310-40  4.7450-80  -0.30  4.7460  4.7260  +14.97 \par USD/RUB 35.810-16  35.966-72  -0.43  35.997  35.763  +17.31 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian forint will remain weaker early this week as the euro-forint cross seems unable to dip below the 300 level in the short term as market sentiment is bleak, one dealer said. The cross is likely to move in a 302-309 range for now. \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  sees some near-term stability in euro-forint, the bank said. The Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rate decision Monday is likely to have a short-lived impact on the forint unless the decision diverges significantly from market expectations for unchanged rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volatility for the zloty is unlikely to disappear but there's a good chance that current levels around 4.75 to the euro can be sustained, said Marcin Bilbin, a dealer with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pekao SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (PEO.WA). "It's not one way street any more," Bilbin said. On Friday, the zloty sustained most of the gains posted after quasi market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday and news that the government had started official talks on ERM2 entry.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Moscow, upcoming month-end tax payments that are to take away an estimated RUB250 billion to RUB350 billion from the money market and tighten liquidity have given the ruble a respite from early-week weakening pressure. Next week's tax payment could allow a minor strengthening of the ruble, but once the month is over and oil prices don't recover, the weakening pressures will return. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded virtually unchanged in the latter days of the week, closing Friday at RUB40.50, some 50 kopecks away from the lower limit of its trading band of RUB41 against a dollar-euro basket.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Czech koruna looks set for more trade in its current, weak level of between 28.5 and 29 to the euro, traders said. "The final word on the koruna will still be regional sentiment, and the weakening Friday of central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't bode well for koruna gains Monday," the trader said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par HUNGARIAN BOND YIELDS - The three-year bond yield was at 13.65% late Friday from 13.40% late Thursday; five-year was at 12.85% from 12.55%; 10-year was at 12% from 11.60%. \par  \par POLISH BOND YIELDS - The two-year average yield was at 5.75% late Friday from 5.70% Thursday; five-year was at 5.93% from 5.86%; 10-year at 6.19% from 6.08%. \par  \par CZECH BOND YIELD - 10-year benchmark at 4.90% late Friday from 4.96% late Thursday. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Polish bonds are moving lower as yields move up amid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility, and Friday thin trade saw most players sidelined watching the volatile zloty and waiting for the Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's meeting Wednesday. Analysts are now expecting only a 25 basis points rate cut instead of 50 basis points a week ago as zloty remains under pressure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungarian government bonds are seen adding further losses amid forint weakening that will be exacerbated Monday if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cuts rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG20                    1383.10   loss   22.8   dn 1.6% \par BUX                     10380.5    loss  269.8   dn 2.5% \par PX                        648.2    loss    8.8   dn 1.4% \par RTS                       517.2    loss   32.0   dn 5.8% \par DJ Stoxx EU Enlarged 15: 1182.68   loss   21.80  dn 1.8% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN WARSAW: While buy orders at the end of Friday's session lifted the index from the 1340-1350 range where it stayed for most of the session, analysts said it's no sign of a trend for the new week given low volumes. Banks remain under pressure: PKO BP ended down 4.7%; BZ WBK lost 4.8%; Pekao down 0.9%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN PRAGUE: Continued negative sentiment should weigh on stocks and keep volumes low Monday, though Telefonica O2, which ended 1.2% higher Friday, may gain Monday ahead of Tuesday's fourth-quarter earnings release. The market expects the company to keep net profit from falling on the year despite the sharp economic slowdown in the quarter. Zentiva closed -1.6% Friday and may move lower in coming days on news its takeover by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sanofi-Aventis\f28 \uc2 \f2  is a done deal. Investors know they'll get CZK1,150 per share from Sanofi regardless of Zentiva's current price.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN BUDAPEST: Some traders expect a big turnaround soon in Budapest, saying liquidity has been building up globally and worries over CEE are overdone. Friday, local stocks clawed back part of the severe, 8% loss seen intraday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 OTP Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  ends unchanged after a temporary suspension for the third time this week for falling over 10% intraday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Magyar Telekom\f28 \uc2 \f2  ended 0.6% after hitting an all-time low.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IN MOSCOW: Russian stock exchanges are closed for a public holiday Monday, but traders expect the market to test recent support levels later in the week. On Friday the benchmark RTS index finished 5.8% higher at 517.22, the fourth negative session of the week, as the somber mood in the U.S. unnerved local investors ahead of the long weekend. Blue chips advanced by 2%-10% with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sberbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norilsk Nickel\f28 \uc2 \f2  hit hardest. [ 02-22-09 2301ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  OTHER NEWS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: The steep fall in the value of eastern European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could create problems for local banks, especially those with high levels of foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exposure, warned a Polish banker, according to the Financial Times. "If the zloty is at the current level over the next six to 12 months and we see an increase in unemployment, then we will see an increase in write-offs," said Krzysztof Rosinski, chief executive of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Getin Holding\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a local banking group that had been one of the most aggressive foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lenders during the recently ended real estate boom, the FT reported on its Web site Sunday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Prime Minister Mirek Topolanek, whose country holds the rotating European Union presidency, said Sunday's talks among Europe's largest economies in Berlin had exposed deep rifts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUSSIA: \f28 \uc2 \f2 USEC Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (USU) said Friday it expects the total amount paid to the Russian Federation for the separative work unit component of low enriched uranium will "substantially" exceed $8 billion by the time the contract, which covers 20 years, is completed in 2013.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Fiscal stimulus programs in industrialized countries should be used to encourage production in ways that are broadly efficient, not narrowly nationalistic, World Bank Europe and Central Asia Chief Economist Indermit Gill said at the launch of the bank's latest EU10 Regular Economic Report in Warsaw on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: The 2009 budget is mainly aimed at preserving and creating jobs through massive public investments in infrastructure, which are the largest after 1989, Romanian Prime Minister Emil Boc told a plenary session of Parliament on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BULGARIA: Bulgarian Property Developments (BPD) PLC Friday announced Windsorville's Offer fails to reflect BPD's net asset value and in particular its significant cash reserves and accordingly, the Board continues to advise shareholders to take no action in respect of their shareholdings in BPD.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Sean Carney, Dow Jones Newswires; +420 222 191 375, sean.carney@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Margit Feher & Edith Balazs in Budapest; David McQuaid & Marek Strzelecki in Warsaw; Andrew Langley & Lidia Kelly in Moscow contributed to the briefing.) [ 02-22-09 2302ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  OTHER NEWS \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Eastern European nations must speak with one voice to refuse protectionism, Poland's foreign minister said Monday amid tension about state aid offered by western EU states to industry.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: The National Bank of Poland (NBP) called on other central and eastern European central banks on Monday to coordinate efforts in countering the dramatic devaluation of the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The recent weakening of the Czech koruna and other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been exaggerated, prompting central and eastern European central banks to step up their cooperation, the governor of the Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday. And the recent weakening of the Czech korunamay force the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lift interest rates, the governor added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUSSIA: EU ministers agreed Monday that Russia and Turkey could take part in some meetings of the bloc's planned "Eastern Partnership," aimed at boosting ties with six former Soviet states.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RUSSIA: Russian billionaire Pyotr Aven is hoping to become Latvia's new prime minister, his adviser said on Monday, a proposal that could stir resentment in a former Soviet republic once ruled from Moscow. Aven, who is of Latvian origin, is the chairman of top Russian lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alfa Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  and has "rich experience" that could help the recession-battered Baltic state, his adviser Alexander Gafin said on Echo of Moscow radio station.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: The Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to act to prevent excessive forint weakness and volatility, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday as part of a coordinated verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the central banks of Central and Eastern Europe.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HUNGARY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \uc2 \f2 Magyar Telekom\f28 \uc2 \f2  Nyrt.'s (MTA) fourth-quarter net profit rose more than analysts had expected as an increase in earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization and a drop in depreciation and amortization expenses were only partly offset by higher income taxes and net financial costs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development is considering a senior loan for up to EUR100 million to Romanian lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banca Comerciala Romana SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  to be lent by BCR to small and medium enterprises in Romania, EBRD said Monday, news agency Mediafax reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: The leu's current exchange rate is sustainable, Romania's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Mugur Isarescu said Monday, news agency Mediafax reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Sean Carney, Dow Jones Newswires; +420 222 191 375, sean.carney@dowjones.com (Margit Feher in Budapest and Malgorzata Halaba & Marek Strzelecki in Warsaw contributed to this briefing.) [ 02-23-09 2301ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020090223e52n0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
