\par\par \b \uc2 Hungary forint firms sharply, dealers eye cbank\b0\par\par\uc2 461 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2009\par 14:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, Feb 4 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint jumped over 1.5 percent to firm past a key level at 300 versus the euro shortly after 1220 GMT on Wednesday, which some dealers said may have been the result of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the unit.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined comment.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not wish to comment," spokeswoman Nora Hevesi told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The forint <EURHUF=D2> firmed from around 302 against the euro to hit a session high at 297 within about 15 minutes.\par \par \uc2 By 1302 GMT it retreated to 298.80 per euro.\par \par \uc2 "Looks like it is an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... Given the force and pace of (downward) pressure everybody says this is an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we will see whether there is any official comment," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. "We have heard from market talk that a German bank, which is not a regular player in the Hungarian market, sold Swiss francs against forints. Dealers believe this is an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," another Budapest-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said.\par \par \uc2 "We believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be behind this." Other dealers said they did not see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and did not believe there was an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I think this is not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I would personally exclude this," a third dealer said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday the excessive volatility of the forint was harmful as it could create stress in the Hungarian financial system.\par \par \uc2 Governor Andras Simor said the bank has the appropriate tools to dampen excessive swings in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "Such fast swings in the exchange rate could create tensions in the domestic financial system, which is undergoing an adjustment anyway, and is therefore more sensitive than normal," Simor was cited by local news agency MTI as saying.\par \par \uc2 He said the bank would "probably add new elements in the near future to its set of tools applied so far", but did not give further details.\par \par \uc2 The forint hit an all-time low of 304 versus the euro earlier on Wednesday and the weak forint is seen hurting Hungarian households who borrowed heavily in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few years.\par \par \uc2 "Since current levels of the forint exchange rate could be very close to the pain threshold of Hungarian households, we think the NBH will continue to try to push EUR/HUF lower by its comments," \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said in note on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "Moreover, further substantial forint depreciation could also trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the NBH would try to limit risks of households' defaults on the back of higher \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  credit repayments," the bank added.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Gergely Szakacs; Editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 HUNGARY-FORINT/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|HX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090204e5240015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
