\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 4- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mixed after Czech rate cut, zloty eases further\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sandor Peto and Marius Zaharia   \par \uc2 1,096 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2008\par 17:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds new details in para 8, last five paras, updates prices.)\par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST/BUCHAREST, Dec 17 (Reuters) - Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed on Wednesday after the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates by 50 basis points to 2.25 percent in the latest move to bolster growth in the region's emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The Czech crown <EURCZK=> moved little after the decision, which was in line with consensus expectations.\par \par \uc2 Other rate cuts are expected to follow in the region, potentially weighing on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but market turnover was moderate as trade wound down toward the year-end.\par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty <EURPLN=> extended losses, while Hungary's forint <EURHUF=> was shielded by a jump by shares on the Budapest bourse due to news that a Middle East investor wants to build a seven percent stake in MOL . [ID:nLH249162]\par \par \uc2 The crown firmed 0.32 percent against the euro by 1522 GMT to 26.26, the zloty shed 1.06 percent to 4.118 and the forint firmed by 0.29 percent to 266.66. Romania's leu <EURRON=> weakened by 0.53 percent to 3.955.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts had speculated the Czech bank could cut by a more aggressive 75 basis points and dealers said the bank was likely to reduce rates further at a gradual pace.\par \par \uc2 "(The decision) was mostly expected," said Dalimil Vyskovsky, bond trader at \uc2 Komercni Banka\uc2 . "I think rates should head lower, but it will be slow as we have done a lot recently."\par \par \uc2 The bank said downside risks to inflation pointed to possible further rate easing. [ID:nLH86292]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region firmed briefly overnight after a deep rate cut by the U.S. Fed. [ID:nN16593807].\par \par \uc2 But analysts said the region remained exposed to the global credit crunch and recession in their main export markets that would help trigger further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said in a note that dollar weakness in the wake of the Fed rate cut was broadly supportive to emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but European emerging markets were "the most vulnerable in a global environment of tight financing".\par \par \uc2 The Polish and Hungarian central banks are expected to cut interest rates again next week.\par \par \uc2 Polish Finance Minister Jacek Rostowski said lower rates would be the best remedy for the economy's slowdown [ID:nWAR007708], while \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Slawomir Skrzypek said he could not rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the zloty's slide. [ID:nLH441308]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint remained steady at levels which dealers said may allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to deliver its third 50 basis point interest rate cut in four weeks next Monday, bringing rates to 10.0 percent.\par \par \uc2 "Views about the possibility of a cut are split even within the room," one Budapest-based dealer said.\par \par \uc2 "I think they can test the market as the forint is stable between 260 and 270... interest rate swaps, bond yields corrected upwards recently but are going down again, I think the majority in the market expects a rate cut."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Andras Simor said the bank had no exchange rate target, but among market factors the exchange rate was a key influence on monetary policy decisions.[ID:nBUD002716]\par \par \uc2 Serbian Deputy Prime Minister Mladjan Dinkic also said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to lower interest rates soon in response to lower price pressures.[ID:nLH622594].\par \par \uc2 In Romania, the leu bucked the trend in early trade but weakened later. Dealers said rumours about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past days had helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it can get further support from news about the incoming government.\par \par \uc2 "The rapid announcement of the new ministries and members should allay any further fears of uncertainty on the part of the coalition parties' commitments to work together to tackle the difficult year ahead," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The Democrat-Liberals and Social Democrats, who have forged a governing coalition, continued their talks on the new government, after posting their draft programme on Tuesday [ID:nLG497383].\par \par \uc2 They are expected to come up with the names of the future ministers on Thursday and a final governing programme on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Anticipations of rate cuts improved sentiment in Poland's and Hungary's government bond markets, yields dropped and traders said prices may extend gains if interest rates are cut. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ----------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT-------------------------\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest   Previous Local    Local\par                                   close    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                                            change   change\par                                            today    in 2008 \par Czech crown      <EURCZK=>   26.263    26.348  +0.32%   +0.88%\par Polish zloty     <EURPLN=>   4.118    4.075   -1.06