\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Emerging Markets-Fall as funds flee, Hungary ups rates\b0\par\par\uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2008\par 11:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Emerging stocks drop over 4 pct to three-year low\par \par \uc2 * Sovereign debt spreads at widest since early 2003\par \par \uc2 * Hungary raises rates after forint hits 2-year low vs euro\par \par \uc2 * Rand at lowest in over 6 years vs dollar * Belarus asks IMF for $2 bln loan\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds fresh comment, money markets, Belarus)\par \par \uc2 By Carolyn Cohn\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 22 (Reuters) - Emerging stocks and bonds slid in a panic sell-off on Wednesday as hedge funds dashed to unwind positions, but Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried to throttle a slide in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a three-percentage point rate rise.\par \par \uc2 The banking crisis that started in developed markets is leading to steep falls in emerging markets, as investors are forced to retrench, analysts and traders say.\par \par \uc2 "There is a need for hedge funds to withdraw from emerging markets to cover redemptions that are occurring, it is a reversal of the carry trade that is being unwound at a very rapid rate," said Neil Dougall, chief emerging markets economist at \uc2 Dresdner Kleinwort\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It's not that the fundamentals for emerging markets have changed. Capital is now moving back from the emerging world to the developed world."\par \par \uc2 Benchmark emerging equities dropped to 553.10 <.MSCIEF> by 1145 GMT, their lowest since June 2005 and down 4.67 percent.\par \par \uc2 Emerging sovereign debt spreads <11EMJ> widened beyond 700 basis points over U.S. Treasuries for the first time since early 2003, and were trading 26 bps wider at 715.\par \par \uc2 The forint hit its lowest in more than two years against the euro <EURHUF=>, but rose sharply after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked rates by three percentage points to 11.50 percent, only two days after it left rates unchanged.\par \par \uc2 "This may provide some short-term support to the forint but overall I think it just adds to the sense of panic," said Nigel Rendell, emerging markets strategist at RBC.\par \par \uc2 "Are people going to hold the forint just because they get an extra 3 percent on it? I don't think so. And of course raising rates makes it harder for local borrowers to repay their loans. It means the economy is toast."\par \par \uc2 The euro has risen as much as 15 percent this month against the forint, its biggest monthly jump since the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's launch in Jan 1999.\par \par \uc2 AFTER \b \highlight22\uc2 HUNGARY\b0 \highlight\uc2 , TURKEY EYED\par \par \uc2 Traders said there was speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the forint ahead of market holidays in Hungary on Thursday and Friday. Prime Minister Ferenc Gyurcsany said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as necessary. [nBSB001668]\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's debt in the five-year credit default swap market rose by around 30 basis points, crossing the 500 bps threshold to 515-545 bps, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira hit its weakest against the dollar <TRY=> since June 2006, while the rand hit its lowest since April 2002 <ZAR=>. Russia's rouble hit a two-year low against the dollar [nLM350135].\par \par \uc2 Analysts speculate that the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may raise interest rates as early as Wednesday's meeting. [nLM481960]\par \par \uc2 However, the Romanian leu bucked the trend, rising 1 percent against the euro <EURRON=> on soaring money market rates in a liquidity shortage. Romanian overnight rates <RONOND=> were showing their highest offer rate in over six years.\par \par \uc2 Amid the global storm, increasing numbers of emerging economies are looking for rescue packages from the International Monetary Fund.\par \par \uc2 Hungarian officials signalled on Wednesday they were in talks with the IMF. [nLM390122]\par \par \uc2 Belarus also said on Wednesday it had requested a $2 billion loan from the IMF. [nLM708734]\par \par \uc2 Iceland and Ukraine are also hoping for IMF aid soon to resuscitate their economies, and IMF and Pakistani officials are meeting in Dubai amid speculation the government will ask for a support package.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Argentina was looking particularly vulnerable after its move on Tuesday to nationalise its pension funds unnerved investors. Five-year credit default swaps, used to insure against restructuring or default of debt, were being quoted at over 3,000 basis points.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Peter Apps and Jamie McGeever; Editing by Andy Bruce)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|G|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PGE|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081025e4am0006o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
