\par\par \b \uc2 Hungary forint volatility persists, region suffers  \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 10:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, March 24 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint moved in a wide range between 265.60 and 263.90 to the euro in early Friday trade, weaker from Thursday, as volatility has remained the order of the day.  \par \par \uc2 At 0855 GMT, the forint <EURHUF=> traded at 264.45/95 to the euro, weaker from 263.70 in late Thursday trade, but firmer than a day-low of 265.60 around 0840 GMT, as markets in the region continued to suffer from the impact of interest rate hikes on core markets.  \par \par \uc2 "London banks moved the forint this morning. The market is very nervous, we are in a rollercoaster because of the interest rate hikes in G7 economies. The CE4 countries are the hardest hit as the market prices the hikes in," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 He said volatility was likely to persist on the forint market, with movements of up to 1-2 percent within a day, and in the near term the forint could ease even beyond a 25-month low around 268 on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "The (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) did not hike rates, saying the medium-term inflation target was not in danger. I think the forint can move easily to 270 before the bank may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in any way," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  left the base rate unchanged at 6.0 percent, the highest in the European Union, at its monthly rate-setting meeting on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond yields were up 1 to 4 basis points. ---------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0855 GMT ----------- EUR/HUF<EURHUF=> eases to 264.45/95 from 263.70/4.00 USD/HUF<HUF=> eases to 220.75/1.05 from 220.06/33 3-yr 2009/E bond yield up 1 bp at 7.09/7.19 pct 5-yr 2011/B bond yield up 4 bps at 7.05/7.15 pct 10-yr 2016/C bond yield up 2 bps at 6.94/7.04 pct --------------------------------------------------------  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-HUNGARY-FORINT/BONDS|LANGEN|HX|ABN|M|D|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060327e23o000mz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
