\par\par \b \uc2 Hungary, Factors to watch and Press Digest July 15  \b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2005\par 08:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, July 15 (Reuters) - Following is a list of events in Hungary and the region, as well as news stories and press reports which may influence financial markets on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The Hungarian press digest is at the end of this item.  \par \par \uc2 (For any queries: Budapest editorial +361 327 4745)  \par \par \uc2 WHAT IS HAPPENING IN HUNGARY ALL TIMES GMT  \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST - Final industrial output, May (0700)  \par \par \uc2 IN THE REGION  \par \par \uc2 WARSAW - Bureau scheduled to interview CEO of PKO Bank Polski , eastern Europe's top lender.  \par \par \uc2 PRAGUE - June monetary base (0800)  \par \par \uc2 PRAGUE - Representatives of parliamentary parties meet to discuss options of pension reform (1200)  \par \par \uc2 BRATISLAVA - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to release its weekly foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data.  \par \par \uc2 IN THE NEWS, REUTERS  \par \par \uc2 Hungary sees July budget surplus, year target on track [nL14577866]  \par \par \uc2 Hungary MOL rejects new Bosnian Energopetrol offer [nL1498805]  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bids for 59,700 T EU \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wheat [nL14142536]  \par \par \uc2 IN THE NEWS, HUNGARIAN PRESS  \par \par \uc2 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  must take on a more powerful role in combating terrorism, Prime Minister Ferenc Gyurcsany told the annual conference for Hungarian ambassadors in Budapest.  \par \par \uc2 - Prime Minister Ferenc Gyurcsany will meet U.S. President George W. Bush at the White House in Washington on October 3.  \par \par \uc2 - Hungary's law enforcement agencies are to work out by September 1 a common plan to minimise the consequences of any terrorist acts, Interior Minister Monika Lampert announced.  \par \par \uc2 - The parliamentary commission investigating the accumulation of wealth by the Orban family became practically dysfunctional after Democratic Forum caucus leader Karoly Herenyi said he will not take part in it so long as Socialist Laszlo Molnar remains its chairman.  \par \par \uc2 - Fidesz chairman Viktor Orban is spending part of his holidays with one of his children in the Colorado mountains as the guest of Hungary's honorary consul Jeno Felegyhazi-Megyesy.  \par \par \uc2 - The four parliamentary parties are willing to hold talks on a draft declaration on Hungary's long-term economic strategy submitted by Economy Minister Janos Koka.  \par \par \uc2 - Lists of Roma pupils were drawn up at a primary school in Kerepes contrary to law, an inquiry by the national and ethnic minorities ombudsman has found. There are an estimated 700,000-800,000 disadvantaged children in Hungary, 60-80 percent of whom are Roma.  \par \par \uc2 - Outgoing Hungarian Radio president Katalin Kondor entrusted vice president Janos Hollos with running day-to-day affairs until her successor is elected by the board of trustees.  \par \par \uc2 - The Finance Ministry is expecting a budget surplus of 29 billion forints for July, Finance Ministry administrative state secretary Tamas Katona announced.  \par \par \uc2 - Almost all analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut the base rate by 25 basis points to 6.75 percent on Monday, according to a survey by Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 - The government is determined to implement the VAT cut and for that, it plans to take certain steps so that consumers benefit from the measure, Finance Minister Janos Veres said.  \par \par \uc2 - The total funds allocated through the EU's Phare development programme was 370 billion forints between 1990 and 2003, which means that companies and local governments applied succesfully for 96 percent of the money earmarked for Hungary, EU Affairs Minister Etele Barath said.  \par \par \uc2 - MOL cannot accept the Bosnian government's request that MOL-INA consortium should pay 15 million euros more for Energopetrol, spokesman Sandor Kator said.  \par \par \uc2 - Sales of passenger cars and trucks were down 10 percent in the first six months, year-on-year, the Hungarian Car Importers Association announced.  \par \par \uc2 - High taxes and the flood of cheap imported beer took its toll on Hungarian breweries in 2004, as the industry's sales fell 11 percent last year.  \par \par \uc2 (Source: taken from Nepszabadsag's Hungary Around the Clock service. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.  \par \par \uc2 To subscribe to Hungary Around the Clock, contact Monica Kovacs at (361) 351 7142 or fax (361) 351 7141.)  \par \par \uc2 HUNGARY-FACTORS|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|HX|REVU|DNP|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050715e17f000he\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
