\par\par \b \uc2 Hungary Fin Min Veres: 2005 GDP, CPI Lower Than Planned  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Marton Dunai and Margit Feher  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 692 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2005\par 16:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--Hungary's newly-appointed Finance Minister Janos Veres said Thursday he won't bow to any pressure to up spending ahead of the 2006 general election.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts worry that the appointment of Veres, an inner circle member of the governing Socialist Party, puts budget targets at risk as the party prepares for the spring 2006 elections.  \par \par \uc2 "(The Socialist Party) won't pressure me to alter fiscal policy just because that would seem to be in its interest ahead of the elections," Veres told Dow Jones Newswires ahead of taking up his role Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "The budget won't be allowed to get out of hand and there is the political will to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's budget are mounting as the finance ministry projects the deficit will reach 70% of its year-end target by the end of April. [ 21-04-05 1426GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 A budget buffer of HUF160 billion guarantees that a deficit overrun can be avoided and a variety of legislative measures are in the works to increase the efficiency of value added tax collection, the minister said.  \par \par \uc2 Each year, HUF210 billion-HUF220 billion in VAT payments remain uncollected as taxpayers exploit loopholes, Veres said, adding that these will soon be closed.  \par \par \uc2 "Under the present conditions I know about at the moment, the budget plans can be and will be met. If oil prices reach $100 (a barrel), we may modify the budget but not because of the elections," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Veres didn't promise sweeping changes in the large redistribution systems such as health care and education in the year before the elections, but said that a series of legislative changes and minor reforms in the financing of those systems are on the table.  \par \par \uc2 "My clout in the Socialist Party will have to be used" to align the party behind that agenda, Veres added. His predecessor Tibor Draskovics was neither a member of the Socialist Party, nor did he enjoy the confidence of Prime Minister Ferenc Gyurcsany, who came to power in September.  \par \par \uc2 Veres, an affluent businessman, declined to give a specific target for the forint, which many investment houses think overvalued.  \par \par \uc2 "For the aspects of economy and the budget there are more favorable levels (than the current HUF248.50 to the euro) but I don't see 280 justified. Of course, it would be nice to step away from levels in the 240s," he said. [ 21-04-05 1440GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Veres said that the strained relationship between the government and the National Bank of Hungary could soon a thing of the past.  \par \par \uc2 "I will respect the independence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and I don't want to butt in on its work. Fiscal policy will create the conditions for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut rates bravely," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Veres and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zsigmond Jarai have known each other from when Jarai was finance minister and Veres sat on the parliamentary finance committee.  \par \par \uc2 The finance minister said he thought a 25 basis point cut in the key interest rate is realistic for the next rate meeting of the bank's monetary council.  \par \par \uc2 Lower interest rates may be supported by falling inflation. Veres said he was confident inflation wasn't dropping too fast, weighing on budget revenue.  \par \par \uc2 "Inflation will be closer to 4.5% than the 3.5% some analysts have forecast," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Veres acknowledged that the European Union's gloomy growth outlook is a risk for Hungary. In 2005 gross domestic product growth will be near 4%, albeit below that figure, but not as low as 3.5%, which he called too pessimistic.  \par \par \uc2 If growth slows, he said the government doesn't plan to boost domestic consumption.  \par \par \uc2 Veres said he didn't plan to increase the government's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing beyond present plans for EUR3 billion this year. Nonetheless, he added that the government was "flexible" on those plans.  \par \par \uc2 -By Marton Dunai and Margit Feher, Dow Jones Newswires; +361-267-0623; marton.dunai@dowjones.com [ 21-04-05 1459GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050421e14l000ny\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (hungary near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\fa